<node id="Java">
  <data key="d0">Java</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Java is a statically typed, strongly typed programming language and platform, identified as a trademark or registered trademark of Sun Microsystems, Inc. in the United States and other countries. It is presented as the eventual language reached after assembly language, C, and C++, and as a modern programming environment with automatic code completion, standard libraries and public APIs documented by Javadocs, and a comparatively wordy syntax because its type system requires many words. Java’s strongly typed objects allow editing environments to detect type errors before compilation, and the proper noun Java appears in terms such as Java Virtual Machine, Java 5, and the java.util.concurrent package.

Java underlies many example source files, code snippets, class listings, package declarations, file names, and JSP files, including the Map, sensor, and generics examples and files such as Stack.java and PrintPrimes.java. Its examples cover image scaling, rotation, and duplication elimination; a Stack; class X illustrating a concurrency challenge; client/server code; payroll and bowling programs, including enums introduced in Java 5; PageIterator; the Modem interface; the toString naming convention; exception handling and error-code definitions; UserValidator; appendFooter; set; a FitNesse source containing HTTP_DATE_REGEXP; GeneratePrimes.java; PrimeGenerator.java; CodeAnalyzer.java; DeviceController and file retrieval code; Collections.emptyList(); and NullPointerException. Java also relates to a line-width distribution figure, demonstrates that source file size is closely tied to class size, and uses a common convention of declaring instance variables at the top of a class; style guidance advises avoiding long import lists and not inheriting constants.

Java 5 is associated with concurrency and development improvements, although Java’s threading model does not guarantee preemptive threading; it offers the synchronized keyword and synchronized methods. Related technical discussions involve byte-code, serialization, classes, interfaces, constants, unit tests, and JUnit, with Kent Beck noted as wanting to learn during early JUnit development. Java supplies date-related programming context through SerialDate, SerialDate.Java, SerialDateTests.java, SpreadsheetDate.java, java.lang.IllegalArgumentException, java.util.Date, and java.util.Calendar; SerialDate represents dates, and Java is listed as one language mixed in SerialDate comments. The Java platform appears in the JCommon header and the environment referenced by SpreadsheetDate.java, where JCommon is a free general-purpose class library for Java, and Java is the language used in the Java/Swing program Sparkle. Java and its platform also host application code, Java proxies, frameworks, byte-code libraries, Java 5 annotations, EJB code, plain old Java objects, the AspectJ extension, the Spring Framework dependency-injection container in which objects are requested by name, the JMock testing context, and standards discussions of class structure and member ordering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d813b42e06df0d7b6f90cb9e254aaf18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-178d6fd5b64909f0f5e42a12e3534440-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-178d6fd5b64909f0f5e42a12e3534440-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-178d6fd5b64909f0f5e42a12e3534440-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-178d6fd5b64909f0f5e42a12e3534440-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-00