<node id="HTML">
  <data key="d0">HTML</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A markup language that may appear in a Java source file or a JSP file.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML is markup used in SerialDate Javadoc comments, and HTML is cited as an undesirable mixing of languages in the source file.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML is the markup format used to render the page in the described code example.&lt;SEP&gt;HTML is the markup output generated by Listing 3-1 and returned or rendered by getHtml and renderPageWithSetupsAndTeardowns.&lt;SEP&gt;A markup output format produced when the refactored function renders a page.</data>
