</node>
<node id="StringBuffer">
  <data key="d0">StringBuffer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Java mutable character sequence class used by unexpectedArgumentMessage to build an unexpected-argument error message.&lt;SEP&gt;StringBuffer is a type discussed as an instance variable that could alternatively be passed as a function argument.&lt;SEP&gt;StringBuffer is a class used as an argument or instance variable in the examples, including includeSetupPageInto and transform.&lt;SEP&gt;StringBuffer is the Java type of the report argument in the appendFooter example, allowing the argument to act as an output argument.&lt;SEP&gt;Buffer used by SetupTeardownIncluder to accumulate new page content.&lt;SEP&gt;StringBuffer is a Java class mentioned as a possible way to make the getState implementation more efficient, although the author often avoids it when the cost is small.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="InputStream">
  <data key="d0">InputStream</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Java input stream type obtained from a socket to read message data in getMessage.&lt;SEP&gt;InputStream is a class returned by fileOpen to represent an opened file stream.&lt;SEP&gt;InputStream is a Java class used as a field in FitNesseExpediter and assigned from a Socket through getInputStream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="String">
  <data key="d0">String</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">String is the Java String class, and the descriptions collectively identify it as the type used for textual arguments, values, messages, and formatted output in several components. In the first draft of Args.java, String is used for schema elements, the command-line argument array, string arguments, and related values. More generally, it represents command-line parameter values and string argument values and parameters in marshaling code; it serves as the argument to the abstract set method in ArgumentMarshaler and as the cast target in GetString. It is also used for schema elements, argument parameters, and formatted error messages.

String is additionally used in formatting, date handling, and messaging. Its static format method is used by reportHours, and the class is used as the target of String.format for date formatting; it is returned by DayDate.toString and Month.toString. In SerialDate.java, String appears as a parameter and return type in month-name and string-parsing methods. In messaging contexts, String is used as the message type in MessageUtils and in the client handler inside the process method.&lt;SEP&gt;String is a type used for a file-name argument in the fileOpen transformation example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OutputStream">
  <data key="d0">OutputStream</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Java output stream type obtained from a socket to write message data in sendMessage.&lt;SEP&gt;OutputStream is a Java class used as a field in FitNesseExpediter and assigned from a Socket through getOutputStream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-004</data>
