<node id="Addison-Wesley">
  <data key="d0">Addison-Wesley</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Addison-Wesley is a publisher associated with a range of software engineering and programming books. In the provided descriptions, it is identified as the publisher of Extreme Programming Explained: Embrace Change, Design Patterns: Elements of Reusable Object Oriented Software, The Pragmatic Programmer, Refactoring: Improving the Design of Existing Code, Implementation Patterns, and Domain Driven Design.

Addison-Wesley is also listed as the publisher of Test Driven Development, Working Effectively with Legacy Code, and XUnit Patterns. Across the source descriptions, it is repeatedly cited in bibliographies as the publishing house for Design Patterns: Elements of Reusable Object Oriented Software and The Pragmatic Programmer, along with the other listed titles.&lt;SEP&gt;A publisher listed for Implementation Patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Addison-Wesley is the publisher of the Design Patterns: Elements of Reusable Object Oriented Software book.&lt;SEP&gt;Addison-Wesley is the publisher listed for Object Design: Roles, Responsibilities, and Collaborations.</data>
