</node>
<node id="C">
  <data key="d0">C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">C is a module reached through B that modules using A should not need to know about.&lt;SEP&gt;C is a programming language mentioned as requiring functions to be defined or declared before they are used.&lt;SEP&gt;C is a programming language mentioned as part of the progression from assembly language toward C++ and Java.&lt;SEP&gt;C is an integer variable in the initial code fragment that tracks the column offset while printing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-003</data>
