<node id="Maintainability">
  <data key="d0">Maintainability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The property of the argument parsing code being compact, simple, reasonably maintainable, or becoming difficult to maintain due to added argument types&lt;SEP&gt;Maintainability is the quality that allows code to be changed, repaired, and improved over time, and maintainability is influenced by coding style and readability.&lt;SEP&gt;Maintainability is a code quality outcome that improves when error handling can be reasoned about independently of main logic.&lt;SEP&gt;A quality of production code preserved by unit tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Maintainability is an attribute of production code that tests preserve and enhance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-07.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606382</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
