<node id="Team">
  <data key="d0">Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Team is the group of programmers or developers that can be dragged down or ground to a crawl by bad code.&lt;SEP&gt;A team is a group of developers who should agree on a single set of formatting rules and comply with those rules.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of people whose internal communications are optimized by agile practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The project development group slowed by messy code, rebelling against low productivity, and demanding a grand redesign.&lt;SEP&gt;An unnamed software team with a burdensome test suite that was eventually discarded.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f8b0f36a5c42d0808fec00a058082be8-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d58f62a4832abf3c8bbf730215895c6d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-11.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-01.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606382</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical Distance">
  <data key="d0">Vertical Distance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vertical distance is the distance between private function invocations and definitions.&lt;SEP&gt;Vertical Distance is a code-formatting principle that states closely related concepts should be kept vertically close in a source file to reduce scrolling and mental effort.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Variables">
  <data key="d0">Local Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Local Variables store unshared data within a thread and help avoid synchronization problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Variables with method or block scope that reduce the chance of synchronization problems in a Servlet.&lt;SEP&gt;Local variables are variables that should be declared just above first usage and should have small vertical scope.&lt;SEP&gt;Local Variables are a naming scope mentioned in the prefix-convention example where the prefix a may be meaningful.&lt;SEP&gt;Local Variables are variables declared within a function that should be declared as close to their usage as possible.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-178d6fd5b64909f0f5e42a12e3534440-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-178d6fd5b64909f0f5e42a12e3534440-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-13.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-02.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
