<node id="Assert">
  <data key="d0">Assert</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A JUnit assertion helper class invoked by ComparisonCompactor to format expected and actual values into a failure message.&lt;SEP&gt;Assert is a class referenced by formatCompactedComparison through the Assert.format call used to produce the final compacted comparison message.&lt;SEP&gt;Assert is a class from JUnit 4.3.1 containing assertTrue and assertFalse methods that share a common naming scheme and similar basic task.&lt;SEP&gt;Assert is a testing statement used to verify behavior, and the number of asserts per concept should be minimized.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
