<node id="compact">
  <data key="d0">compact</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The compact function returns a formatted assertion message and may not compact strings when canBeCompacted returns false, hiding an error-check side effect behind a compact-only name.&lt;SEP&gt;The compact method of ComparisonCompactor compacts comparison failure messages by handling null values, checking string equality, computing common prefix and suffix lengths, and formatting expected and actual values.&lt;SEP&gt;compact is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that constructs a compacted representation of a string by appending ellipses, context fragments, delta markers, and the differing middle fragment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="compactString">
  <data key="d0">compactString</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The compactString helper method produces a compacted form of a string value and is applied to expected and actual.&lt;SEP&gt;The compactString method of ComparisonCompactor builds a compacted string from a source string by wrapping the differing substring in delta markers and appending common prefix and suffix contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;compactString is an earlier string compaction function described as composing a common prefix, a delta start marker, a differing middle fragment, a delta end marker, and a common suffix.&lt;SEP&gt;compactString assembles the compacted result from prefix, changed substring, delta markers, and suffix fragments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="findCommonPrefix">
  <data key="d0">findCommonPrefix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The findCommonPrefix method calculates the common prefix of expected and actual and either returns or sets prefixIndex depending on the refactoring stage.&lt;SEP&gt;The findCommonPrefix method of ComparisonCompactor calculates the length of the common prefix between the expected and actual strings.&lt;SEP&gt;findCommonPrefix is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that computes the length of the leading characters shared by the expected and actual strings.&lt;SEP&gt;findCommonPrefix iterates over expected and actual until characters differ and records the common prefix length.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="findCommonSuffix">
  <data key="d0">findCommonSuffix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The findCommonSuffix method calculates the common suffix of expected and actual and either returns or sets suffixIndex; an intermediate version depends on prefixIndex being already calculated.&lt;SEP&gt;The findCommonSuffix method of ComparisonCompactor calculates the length of the common suffix between the expected and actual strings.&lt;SEP&gt;findCommonSuffix is the original method that is renamed to findCommonPrefixAndSuffix during the refactoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="computeCommonPrefix">
  <data key="d0">computeCommonPrefix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The computeCommonPrefix method of ComparisonCompactor computes the prefix context to display before the differing segment, adding an ellipsis when the prefix exceeds the context length.&lt;SEP&gt;computeCommonPrefix produces the prefix fragment used by compactString.&lt;SEP&gt;computeCommonPrefix is a method invoked by compactString to supply the common prefix fragment before the DELTA_START marker in the earlier string compaction expression.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="computeCommonSuffix">
  <data key="d0">computeCommonSuffix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The computeCommonSuffix method of ComparisonCompactor computes the suffix context to display after the differing segment, adding an ellipsis when the suffix exceeds the context length.&lt;SEP&gt;computeCommonSuffix produces the suffix fragment using expected, suffixLength, contextLength, and ELLIPSIS.&lt;SEP&gt;computeCommonSuffix is a method invoked by compactString to supply the common suffix fragment after the DELTA_END marker in the earlier string compaction expression.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="areStringsEqual">
  <data key="d0">areStringsEqual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The areStringsEqual method of ComparisonCompactor determines whether the expected string equals the actual string.&lt;SEP&gt;A string-equality helper method referenced by canBeCompacted to check whether expected and actual are equal before compaction is allowed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Assert.format">
  <data key="d0">Assert.format</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Assert.format utility formats an assertion message with supplied expected and actual values and is used to return the comparison message.&lt;SEP&gt;The Assert.format method formats a message with expected and actual values for JUnit assertion failure output and is invoked by ComparisonCompactor.&lt;SEP&gt;Assert.format is a formatting method invoked by formatCompactedComparison to format a message using the compact expected and compact actual strings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
