<node id="Math Class">
  <data key="d0">Math Class</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Math Class is a Java standard library class used by CompactString Method for minimum and maximum calculations in substring boundary logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expected Field">
  <data key="d0">Expected Field</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Expected Field is a string member variable of ComparisonCompactor, renamed from fExpected, representing the expected value in assertion comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actual Field">
  <data key="d0">Actual Field</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Actual Field is a string member variable of ComparisonCompactor, renamed from fActual, representing the actual value in assertion comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prefix Field">
  <data key="d0">Prefix Field</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Prefix Field is an integer member variable of ComparisonCompactor used to store the common prefix length.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suffix Field">
  <data key="d0">Suffix Field</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Suffix Field is an integer member variable of ComparisonCompactor used to store the common suffix length.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ContextLength Field">
  <data key="d0">ContextLength Field</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">ContextLength Field is an integer member variable of ComparisonCompactor, renamed from ctxt, used to limit displayed context around differences.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F Prefix">
  <data key="d0">F Prefix</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">F Prefix is a naming convention that prefixes member variables with f to indicate scope, considered redundant in modern environments and removed from the ComparisonCompactor module.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scope Encoding">
  <data key="d0">Scope Encoding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scope Encoding is a practice of encoding variable scope through variable names, such as prefixes, and is described as redundant in modern environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="fExpected Field">
  <data key="d0">fExpected Field</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">fExpected Field is a member variable of the original ComparisonCompactor, named fExpected, that was renamed to the expected member variable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unencapsulated Conditional">
  <data key="d0">Unencapsulated Conditional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unencapsulated Conditional is a code issue in which a conditional at the beginning of the Compact Method is not represented by an explanatory method, making intent less clear.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Negative Conditional">
  <data key="d0">Negative Conditional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Negative Conditional is a conditional expressed in negative form, described as slightly harder to understand than a positive form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Invert Conditional">
  <data key="d0">Invert Conditional</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Invert Conditional is a refactoring or design technique that changes a conditional from negative to positive form to improve understandability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambiguous Variable Names">
  <data key="d0">Ambiguous Variable Names</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambiguous Variable Names is a naming issue in the Compact Method where local variables have the same names as member variables, making their represented values unclear.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Misleading Function Name">
  <data key="d0">Misleading Function Name</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Misleading Function Name is a naming issue in which the Compact Method name compact suggests compaction, although the method may return an unformatted message when compacting is not performed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="String Class">
  <data key="d0">String Class</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">String Class is a Java standard library class used by ComparisonCompactor to represent expected, actual, and compacted text values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="formatCompactedComparison">
  <data key="d0">formatCompactedComparison</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The formatCompactedComparison method is a proposed replacement for the compact function; it accepts a message, calls canBeCompacted, and returns either a formatted compacted comparison or a formatted original comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;formatCompactedComparison is a public method of ComparisonCompactor that formats a compacted comparison message by checking eligibility, computing common prefix and suffix, compacting strings, and delegating to Assert.format.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="canBeCompacted">
  <data key="d0">canBeCompacted</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The canBeCompacted method reports whether compaction is possible by checking that expected and actual are not null and are not equal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="compactExpectedAndActual">
  <data key="d0">compactExpectedAndActual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The compactExpectedAndActual method performs string compaction by calculating common prefix and suffix information and assigning compactExpected and compactActual from compactString results.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="findCommonPrefixAndSuffix">
  <data key="d0">findCommonPrefixAndSuffix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The findCommonPrefixAndSuffix method combines common prefix and suffix calculation to make the ordering between prefix and suffix computation explicit.&lt;SEP&gt;findCommonPrefixAndSuffix is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that computes the common prefix and common suffix lengths between expected and actual strings.&lt;SEP&gt;findCommonPrefixAndSuffix first calls findCommonPrefix and then determines the common suffix length with helper methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="compactExpected">
  <data key="d0">compactExpected</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The compactExpected member variable stores the compacted form of expected and is read when formatting the compacted comparison.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="compactActual">
  <data key="d0">compactActual</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The compactActual member variable stores the compacted form of actual and is read when formatting the compacted comparison.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="prefixIndex">
  <data key="d0">prefixIndex</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The prefixIndex value represents the index where the common prefix of expected and actual ends.&lt;SEP&gt;prefixIndex is the original common prefix counter initialized in findCommonPrefix before length-based naming is discussed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="suffixIndex">
  <data key="d0">suffixIndex</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The suffixIndex value represents the length or index information for the common suffix of expected and actual.&lt;SEP&gt;suffixIndex is the original one-based common suffix variable before renaming to suffixLength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidden Side Effect">
  <data key="d0">Hidden Side Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hidden side effect refers to behavior concealed by the compact function name, including an error check and returning a formatted message rather than only compacted strings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistent Conventions">
  <data key="d0">Consistent Conventions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistent conventions refer to making similar methods return prefix and suffix values rather than mixing return values with member-variable assignment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Function Naming">
  <data key="d0">Function Naming</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Function naming is the concern of choosing method names that accurately reflect behavior, side effects, and returned values, motivating the formatCompactedComparison name.&lt;SEP&gt;The practice of choosing function names to explain function intent, argument intent, and argument order.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Prefix">
  <data key="d0">Common Prefix</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The identical leading characters shared by expected and actual, represented by prefixIndex in the compaction logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Common Suffix">
  <data key="d0">Common Suffix</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The identical trailing characters shared by expected and actual, represented by suffixIndex in the compaction logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Arbitrary Argument">
  <data key="d0">Arbitrary Argument</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The critique that passing prefixIndex to findCommonSuffix is arbitrary because it establishes an execution order without explaining why that order is required.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="charFromEnd">
  <data key="d0">charFromEnd</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">charFromEnd is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that returns a character from a string at an offset counted from the end of the string.&lt;SEP&gt;charFromEnd returns a character from the end of a string for suffix comparison.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="suffixOverlapsPrefix">
  <data key="d0">suffixOverlapsPrefix</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">suffixOverlapsPrefix is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that tests whether the current suffix length would overlap the previously computed prefix length.&lt;SEP&gt;suffixOverlapsPrefix determines whether a candidate suffix would overlap the prefix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="prefixLength">
  <data key="d0">prefixLength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">prefixLength stores the common prefix length used in compactString and overlap checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="suffixLength">
  <data key="d0">suffixLength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">suffixLength stores the common suffix length after replacing the one-based suffixIndex.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="contextLength">
  <data key="d0">contextLength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">contextLength determines the amount of trailing context retained in the compact suffix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DELTA_START">
  <data key="d0">DELTA_START</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DELTA_START is a marker inserted before the changed substring.&lt;SEP&gt;DELTA_START is a string constant defined in ComparisonCompactor with the value "[", used to mark the beginning of the differing middle fragment in compacted comparison output.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DELTA_END">
  <data key="d0">DELTA_END</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DELTA_END is a marker inserted after the changed substring.&lt;SEP&gt;DELTA_END is a string constant defined in ComparisonCompactor with the value "]", used to mark the end of the differing middle fragment in compacted comparison output.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ELLIPSIS">
  <data key="d0">ELLIPSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">ELLIPSIS is an ellipsis marker appended when the compact suffix omits text.&lt;SEP&gt;ELLIPSIS is a string constant defined in ComparisonCompactor with the value "...", used to indicate omitted text when a common prefix or suffix exceeds the configured context length.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Listing 15-4">
  <data key="d0">Listing 15-4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Listing 15-4 is the interim code listing for ComparisonCompactor.java showing the refactored methods and variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Refactoring">
  <data key="d0">Code Refactoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Code Refactoring is the process of renaming methods and variables and simplifying logic to improve the code.&lt;SEP&gt;Process of massaging code by splitting functions, changing names, eliminating duplication, shrinking methods, reordering methods, and breaking out classes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero-Based">
  <data key="d0">Zero-Based</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zero-Based describes the corrected suffix length convention replacing one-based indexing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-Based">
  <data key="d0">One-Based</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One-Based describes the original suffixIndex convention that caused +1 adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero Length Suffix">
  <data key="d0">Zero Length Suffix</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Zero Length Suffix is the empty suffix condition that the suffix guard prevents from being appended.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prefix Length Guard">
  <data key="d0">Prefix Length Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prefix Length Guard is the conditional statement in the interim compactString that prepends the prefix fragment when prefixLength is positive.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suffix Length Guard">
  <data key="d0">Suffix Length Guard</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Suffix Length Guard is the conditional statement in the interim compactString that appends the suffix fragment when suffixLength is positive.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="shouldBeCompacted">
  <data key="d0">shouldBeCompacted</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">shouldBeCompacted is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that determines whether compaction is appropriate by negating the result of shouldNotBeCompacted.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="shouldNotBeCompacted">
  <data key="d0">shouldNotBeCompacted</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">shouldNotBeCompacted is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that identifies conditions under which compaction is unnecessary, including null values or equal expected and actual strings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="delta">
  <data key="d0">delta</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">delta is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that extracts the substring between the common prefix and common suffix, representing the differing middle portion of a string.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="startingEllipsis">
  <data key="d0">startingEllipsis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">startingEllipsis is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that returns an ellipsis when the common prefix length exceeds the configured context length.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="startingContext">
  <data key="d0">startingContext</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">startingContext is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that extracts a leading context fragment from the end of the common prefix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="endingContext">
  <data key="d0">endingContext</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">endingContext is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that extracts a trailing context fragment from the beginning of the region after the common suffix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="endingEllipsis">
  <data key="d0">endingEllipsis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">endingEllipsis is a private method of ComparisonCompactor that returns an ellipsis when the common suffix length exceeds the configured context length.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analysis Functions">
  <data key="d0">Analysis Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis Functions are the group of ComparisonCompactor functions that perform inspection tasks such as determining compaction eligibility, common prefixes, common suffixes, and overlap conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthesis Functions">
  <data key="d0">Synthesis Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthesis Functions are the group of ComparisonCompactor functions that perform construction tasks such as building compacted strings, context fragments, and ellipsis fragments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="StringBuilder">
  <data key="d0">StringBuilder</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">StringBuilder is a class used by compact to append ellipsis, context, delta markers, delta fragment, and ending context before converting the result to a string.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-17d57202bcc8986bfbb2e844fedcd248-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-15.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790594567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chapter 17: Smells and Heuristics">
  <data key="d0">Chapter 17: Smells and Heuristics</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A chapter presenting a list of code smells, pearls, and heuristics for evaluating and refactoring software code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Smells">
  <data key="d0">Code Smells</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A collection of warning signs in source code that indicate potential problems and opportunities for refactoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C1: Inappropriate Information">
  <data key="d0">C1: Inappropriate Information</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a comment holds information better stored in source code control, issue tracking, or other record-keeping systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C2: Obsolete Comment">
  <data key="d0">C2: Obsolete Comment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a comment has become old, irrelevant, or incorrect and should be updated or removed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C3: Redundant Comment">
  <data key="d0">C3: Redundant Comment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a comment restates information that the code already adequately describes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C4: Poorly Written Comment">
  <data key="d0">C4: Poorly Written Comment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a comment is not written carefully, clearly, briefly, or with correct grammar and punctuation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C5: Commented-Out Code">
  <data key="d0">C5: Commented-Out Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where disabled code remains in a source file, rots, and distracts readers, even though source control preserves previous versions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environment">
  <data key="d0">Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of code smells related to build and test processes in a development environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="E1: Build Requires More Than One Step">
  <data key="d0">E1: Build Requires More Than One Step</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where building a project requires many steps, commands, checkouts, or artifacts instead of a single simple operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="E2: Tests Require More Than One Step">
  <data key="d0">E2: Tests Require More Than One Step</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where running all unit tests requires more than one simple command or one button click.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F1: Too Many Arguments">
  <data key="d0">F1: Too Many Arguments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a function has more than a small number of arguments, with more than three being very questionable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F2: Output Arguments">
  <data key="d0">F2: Output Arguments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where function arguments are used as outputs rather than inputs, contrary to reader expectations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F3: Flag Arguments">
  <data key="d0">F3: Flag Arguments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a function takes a Boolean argument that indicates the function does more than one thing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F4: Dead Function">
  <data key="d0">F4: Dead Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A code smell where a method or function is never called and should be discarded.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General">
  <data key="d0">General</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of code smells related to general source file or language usage issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G1: Multiple Languages in One Source File">
  <data key="d0">G1: Multiple Languages in One Source File</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A general code smell involving the use of multiple languages within one source file.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Issue Tracking System">
  <data key="d0">Issue Tracking System</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A record-keeping system for issues, referenced as an alternative place for metadata instead of comments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
