<node id="Logical Dependency">
  <data key="d0">Logical Dependency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Logical Dependency is an assumed or unexplicit dependency between modules that the Make Logical Dependencies Physical rule warns against.&lt;SEP&gt;Logical Dependency is the assumption that HourlyReporter makes about HourlyReport-Formatter's ability to handle page sizes of 55.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical Dependency">
  <data key="d0">Physical Dependency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Physical Dependency is an explicit dependency in which a module asks another module for needed information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Explanatory Variable">
  <data key="d0">Explanatory Variable</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Explanatory Variable is a variable with a meaningful name that holds an intermediate value to make program logic more readable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intermediate Value">
  <data key="d0">Intermediate Value</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate Value is a calculation step that is stored in a named variable as part of using explanatory variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key">
  <data key="d0">Key</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Key is an explanatory variable in the FitNesse Java example that holds the first matched group from a header line.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Value">
  <data key="d0">Value</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Value is an explanatory variable in the FitNesse Java example that holds the second matched group from a header line.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Headers">
  <data key="d0">Headers</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Headers is a data structure in the FitNesse Java example that stores header entries by lowercased key and value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Matched Group">
  <data key="d0">Matched Group</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Matched Group is a captured portion of a matched line, where the first group becomes Key and the second group becomes Value in the FitNesse example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
