<node id="Page">
  <data key="d0">Page</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Page is the list of LineItem objects held by HourlyReporter and printed when the page reaches PAGE_SIZE.&lt;SEP&gt;Page is a web document read from a URL and parsed to accumulate statistics before a summary report is printed.&lt;SEP&gt;Page is a web page retrieved and parsed by PageReader and returned by PageIterator.&lt;SEP&gt;Page is the object passed to deletePage and related deletion operations in the error-code example.&lt;SEP&gt;Page is a domain object in the example code representing a page to be deleted.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HourlyReport-Formatter">
  <data key="d0">HourlyReport-Formatter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HourlyReport-Formatter is a class responsible for formatting the output produced by HourlyReporter and for handling page sizes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getMaxPageSize">
  <data key="d0">getMaxPageSize</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getMaxPageSize is a method proposed for HourlyReport-Formatter that returns the maximum page size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prefer Polymorphism to If/Else or Switch/Case">
  <data key="d0">Prefer Polymorphism to If/Else or Switch/Case</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prefer Polymorphism to If/Else or Switch/Case is heuristic G23, which recommends considering polymorphism before using if/else or switch/case control flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One Switch Rule">
  <data key="d0">One Switch Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One Switch Rule is a rule under heuristic G23 that allows at most one switch statement for a given type of selection and requires its cases to create polymorphic objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Switch Statement">
  <data key="d0">Switch Statement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Switch Statement is a control structure discussed by heuristic G23 and restricted by the One Switch Rule.&lt;SEP&gt;A switch statement is a control construct that by nature handles multiple cases and tends to perform multiple things.&lt;SEP&gt;Switch Statement is a control structure discussed as problematic when duplicated, but tolerable when hidden behind inheritance to create polymorphic objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="If/Else">
  <data key="d0">If/Else</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">If/Else is a conditional control structure contrasted with polymorphism in heuristic G23.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Follow Standard Conventions">
  <data key="d0">Follow Standard Conventions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Follow Standard Conventions is heuristic G24, which requires each team member to follow agreed coding conventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Replace Magic Numbers with Named Constants">
  <data key="d0">Replace Magic Numbers with Named Constants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Replace Magic Numbers with Named Constants is heuristic G25, which recommends hiding raw numbers and other non-self-describing tokens behind named constants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magic Number">
  <data key="d0">Magic Number</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Magic Number is a term for any token whose value is not self-describing, including numbers and string values such as employee names.&lt;SEP&gt;Magic Number is a code token with a non-self-describing value whose meaning and intent are not obvious from the code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Named Constant">
  <data key="d0">Named Constant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Named Constant is a named symbol used to hide a literal value and make the intent of code clearer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SECONDS_PER_DAY">
  <data key="d0">SECONDS_PER_DAY</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">SECONDS_PER_DAY is a named constant that should hide the raw value 86,400 seconds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LINES_PER_PAGE">
  <data key="d0">LINES_PER_PAGE</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">LINES_PER_PAGE is a named constant that should hide the raw value 55 lines per page.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FEET_PER_MILE">
  <data key="d0">FEET_PER_MILE</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">FEET_PER_MILE is a named constant that could hide the well-known raw value 5280 feet per mile.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WORK_HOURS_PER_DAY">
  <data key="d0">WORK_HOURS_PER_DAY</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">WORK_HOURS_PER_DAY is a named constant that could hide the raw value 8 work hours per day.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TWO">
  <data key="d0">TWO</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">TWO is a proposed named constant for the value 2 in the circumference example and is considered unnecessary.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Math.PI">
  <data key="d0">Math.PI</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Math.PI is a predefined constant for the mathematical value pi that is used to avoid raw approximations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="John Doe">
  <data key="d0">John Doe</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">John Doe is an employee named in the assertion example and is identified as employee number 7777.&lt;SEP&gt;John Doe is a person name used as a magic number in the Java assertion and identifies employee number 7777 in a test database.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Employee Number 7777">
  <data key="d0">Employee Number 7777</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Employee Number 7777 is the numeric employee identifier used in the assertion example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page Size">
  <data key="d0">Page Size</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Page Size is the page capacity that HourlyReporter assumes it knows and that should be the responsibility of HourlyReport-Formatter; PAGE_SIZE represents a value of 55.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Misplaced Responsibility">
  <data key="d0">Misplaced Responsibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Misplaced Responsibility is guideline G17 describing that the declaration of PAGE_SIZE in HourlyReporter places page-size responsibility in the wrong class.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raw Number">
  <data key="d0">Raw Number</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Raw Number is a numeric literal in source code that is not hidden behind a well-named constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Listing 17-1">
  <data key="d0">Listing 17-1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Listing 17-1 is a code listing on page 299 that continues HourlyReporter.java and shows the end of the HourlyReporter class with LineItem.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="7777">
  <data key="d0">7777</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">7777 is a numeric magic number used as the expected employee number in the Java assertion example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Database">
  <data key="d0">Test Database</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Test Database is a well-known test database created by a team and preloaded with employee records having known values and attributes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hourly Employee">
  <data key="d0">Hourly Employee</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hourly Employee is the role or classification of the sole employee represented by John Doe in the Test Database.&lt;SEP&gt;Hourly Employee is one employee type handled by the CalculatePay switch statement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HOURLY_EMPLOYEE_ID">
  <data key="d0">HOURLY_EMPLOYEE_ID</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HOURLY_EMPLOYEE_ID is a named constant used to replace the magic number 7777 and identify the expected employee number for the hourly employee.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HOURLY_EMPLOYEE_NAME">
  <data key="d0">HOURLY_EMPLOYEE_NAME</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">HOURLY_EMPLOYEE_NAME is a named constant used to replace the magic number John Doe and identify the hourly employee by name.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G26: Be Precise">
  <data key="d0">G26: Be Precise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G26: Be Precise is a coding guideline requiring explicit, careful decisions about nulls, currency, concurrent updates, query results, and code precision.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Currency">
  <data key="d0">Currency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Currency is a monetary value domain for which the guideline recommends integer representation and appropriate rounding rather than floating point numbers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locking Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Locking Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Locking Mechanism is a concurrency control structure recommended when concurrent updates are possible.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G27: Structure over Convention">
  <data key="d0">G27: Structure over Convention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G27: Structure over Convention is a coding guideline that prefers code structures forcing compliance over naming conventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Switch/Case">
  <data key="d0">Switch/Case</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Switch/Case is a control structure considered less reliable than base classes for enforcing consistent design decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enumeration">
  <data key="d0">Enumeration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enumeration is a named constant structure mentioned in connection with switch/case statements as an approach inferior to base classes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G28: Encapsulate Conditionals">
  <data key="d0">G28: Encapsulate Conditionals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G28: Encapsulate Conditionals is a coding guideline recommending extraction of functions that explain the intent of Boolean conditionals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conditional">
  <data key="d0">Conditional</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conditional is an if or while condition whose Boolean logic can be difficult to understand without encapsulating the intent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G29: Avoid Negative Conditionals">
  <data key="d0">G29: Avoid Negative Conditionals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G29: Avoid Negative Conditionals is a coding guideline recommending that conditionals be expressed positively when possible.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G30: Functions Should Do One Thing">
  <data key="d0">G30: Functions Should Do One Thing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G30: Functions Should Do One Thing is a coding guideline requiring functions to perform a single responsibility rather than multiple sequential operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pay">
  <data key="d0">pay</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">pay is a Java function that initially performs multiple employee payment operations and is later refactored into smaller single-purpose functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="payIfNecessary">
  <data key="d0">payIfNecessary</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">payIfNecessary is a Java function extracted to check whether an employee is due for payment and delegate further processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="calculateAndDeliverPay">
  <data key="d0">calculateAndDeliverPay</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">calculateAndDeliverPay is a Java function extracted to calculate pay for an employee and deliver the calculated pay.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G31: Hidden Temporal Couplings">
  <data key="d0">G31: Hidden Temporal Couplings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G31: Hidden Temporal Couplings is a coding guideline stating that necessary call order dependencies should be made explicit rather than hidden.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MoogDiver">
  <data key="d0">MoogDiver</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MoogDiver is a Java class used to demonstrate hidden temporal couplings among methods that must be called in a specific order.&lt;SEP&gt;MoogDiver is a Java class whose dive method creates a bucket brigade and makes temporal coupling between operations explicit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient">
  <data key="d0">Gradient</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gradient is a component in MoogDiver that must be saturated before splines can be reticulated.&lt;SEP&gt;Gradient is a code type representing the saturated gradient result produced by saturateGradient and consumed by reticulateSplines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spline">
  <data key="d0">Spline</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Spline is a component in MoogDiver that must be reticulated before the moog dive can occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Spline is a code type representing spline values produced by reticulateSplines and consumed by diveForMoog.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="saturateGradient">
  <data key="d0">saturateGradient</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">saturateGradient is a method that prepares a Gradient and must be called before reticulateSplines in the MoogDiver example.&lt;SEP&gt;saturateGradient is a method that produces a Gradient and must be called before reticulateSplines to avoid an UnsaturatedGradientException.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="reticulateSplines">
  <data key="d0">reticulateSplines</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">reticulateSplines is a method that depends on a saturated Gradient and produces or prepares Splines for the MoogDiver dive.&lt;SEP&gt;reticulateSplines is a method that consumes a Gradient and produces a list of Spline values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="diveForMoog">
  <data key="d0">diveForMoog</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">diveForMoog is a method that performs the dive using reticulated Splines and a reason.&lt;SEP&gt;diveForMoog is a method that consumes a list of Spline values and a reason string to complete the MoogDiver operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UnsaturatedGradientException">
  <data key="d0">UnsaturatedGradientException</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">UnsaturatedGradientException is an exception that can occur when reticulateSplines is called before saturateGradient.&lt;SEP&gt;UnsaturatedGradientException is an exception caused when reticulateSplines is called before saturateGradient has been called.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Floating Point Number">
  <data key="d0">Floating Point Number</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Floating Point Number is a numeric representation described as almost criminal when used to represent currency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integer">
  <data key="d0">Integer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Integer is a numeric type recommended for currency representation with appropriate rounding.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer is a Java type used in the Args.java first draft for integer argument values stored in a map keyed by Character.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer is the Java Integer type used as the cast target in GetInt.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer is a Java type representing integer values and providing parsing functionality for String input.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer is a Java class used by IntegerArgumentMarshaler through Integer.parseInt to convert a String parameter to an integer.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer is the Java class whose parse method, referenced as Integer.parseInt, is used by stringToMonthCode to parse numeric month code strings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rounding">
  <data key="d0">Rounding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Rounding is an arithmetic adjustment that should be handled appropriately when dealing with currency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transaction Management">
  <data key="d0">Transaction Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Transaction Management is a concurrency control mechanism mentioned alongside locks for possible concurrent updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ArrayList">
  <data key="d0">ArrayList</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ArrayList is a Java collection type that is considered overly constraining when a List declaration would do.&lt;SEP&gt;ArrayList is a Java collection type used for the listeners field of ContainerBase in Tomcat.&lt;SEP&gt;Java collection class used to initialize the list that collects Java source files&lt;SEP&gt;ArrayList is a Java collection class instantiated and returned by retrieveSection as an empty list of RecordedGrip.&lt;SEP&gt;ArrayList is a Java collection type used by PrimeGenerator to store prime factor multiples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-04.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-07.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boolean Logic">
  <data key="d0">Boolean Logic</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Boolean Logic is conditional logic in if or while statements that is difficult to understand without intent-explaining functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query">
  <data key="d0">Query</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Query is a database operation whose first match should not be assumed to be the only match.&lt;SEP&gt;Query is an operation that answers a question about an object without changing its state, as in attributeExists, and is the other side of Command Query Separation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Record">
  <data key="d0">Record</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Record is a database item for which code should verify whether it is the only matching record.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Disagreement">
  <data key="d0">Disagreement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Disagreement is identified as a possible cause of ambiguity and imprecision in code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laziness">
  <data key="d0">Laziness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Laziness is identified as a possible cause of ambiguity and imprecision in code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Naming Convention">
  <data key="d0">Naming Convention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Naming Convention is a good but inferior alternative to structures that force compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Naming Convention is a convention that allows multiple words to be easily read in function names and helps give functions descriptive names.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design Decision">
  <data key="d0">Design Decision</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design Decision is a decision that should be enforced with structure rather than convention.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moog">
  <data key="d0">Moog</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Moog is the target of the dive in the MoogDiver example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Employee.find">
  <data key="d0">Employee.find</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Employee.find is a static lookup method that retrieves an Employee by name.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="employeeNumber">
  <data key="d0">employeeNumber</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">employeeNumber is a method that returns an Employee number.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="deliverPay">
  <data key="d0">deliverPay</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">deliverPay is a method that delivers a calculated Money value to an Employee.&lt;SEP&gt;deliverPay is an abstract method associated with Employee that delivers a Money amount to an employee.&lt;SEP&gt;deliverPay is an abstract method of Employee that delivers pay and can be dispatched polymorphically through Employee.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isPayday">
  <data key="d0">isPayday</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">isPayday is a method that checks whether an Employee is due for pay.&lt;SEP&gt;isPayday is an abstract boolean method associated with Employee that indicates whether the current day is a payday.&lt;SEP&gt;isPayday is an abstract method of Employee that determines whether a date is a payday and can be dispatched polymorphically through Employee.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="shouldBeDeleted">
  <data key="d0">shouldBeDeleted</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">shouldBeDeleted is an extracted function that explains whether a Timer should be deleted.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="hasExpired">
  <data key="d0">hasExpired</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">hasExpired is a method that checks whether a Timer has expired.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isRecurrent">
  <data key="d0">isRecurrent</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">isRecurrent is a method that checks whether a Timer is recurrent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="shouldCompact">
  <data key="d0">shouldCompact</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">shouldCompact is a positive conditional method used to check whether a Buffer should compact.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="shouldNotCompact">
  <data key="d0">shouldNotCompact</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">shouldNotCompact is a negative conditional method used to check whether a Buffer should not compact.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="dive">
  <data key="d0">dive</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">dive is a method in MoogDiver that calls saturateGradient, reticulateSplines, and diveForMoog in a dependent sequence.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bucket Brigade">
  <data key="d0">Bucket Brigade</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bucket Brigade is a pattern in which each function produces a result needed by the next function, preventing out-of-order calls.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Don't Be Arbitrary">
  <data key="d0">Don't Be Arbitrary</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Don't Be Arbitrary is a guideline that code structure should have a communicated reason and should not place public classes arbitrarily inside other classes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AliasLinkWidget">
  <data key="d0">AliasLinkWidget</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AliasLinkWidget is a Java class in FitNesse that extends ParentWidget and was used to illustrate arbitrary nested class placement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ParentWidget">
  <data key="d0">ParentWidget</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ParentWidget is a class extended by AliasLinkWidget.&lt;SEP&gt;ParentWidget is a Java class type used in a test to hold a BoldWidget instance as the parent widget.&lt;SEP&gt;ParentWidget is a Java class referenced as the superclass of BoldWidget.&lt;SEP&gt;ParentWidget is a software class used as a constructor parameter of CommentWidget and passed to the superclass constructor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-04.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-05.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VariableExpandingWidgetRoot">
  <data key="d0">VariableExpandingWidgetRoot</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VariableExpandingWidgetRoot is a public static class nested inside AliasLinkWidget although it had no need to be scoped there.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encapsulate Boundary Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Encapsulate Boundary Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Encapsulate Boundary Conditions is a guideline that boundary-condition processing should be placed in one location instead of scattered through code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fit">
  <data key="d0">Fit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Fit is a software example source referenced for a boundary-condition snippet involving Parse and tags.length.&lt;SEP&gt;An artifact invented by Ward Cunningham.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d58f62a4832abf3c8bbf730215895c6d-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-01.txt</data>
