<node id="Boundary Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Boundary Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Boundary Conditions are edge-case checks in code, such as checking level + 1 against tags.length, that are difficult to keep consistent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="nextLevel">
  <data key="d0">nextLevel</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">nextLevel is a variable that encapsulates the expression level + 1 in the boundary-condition example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functions Should Descend Only One Level of Abstraction">
  <data key="d0">Functions Should Descend Only One Level of Abstraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Functions Should Descend Only One Level of Abstraction is a guideline that statements within a function should all be at the same abstraction level, one level below the function name.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HruleWidget">
  <data key="d0">HruleWidget</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HruleWidget is a module in FitNesse that detects a row of four or more dashes and converts it into an Hr Tag with a size based on extra dashes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="render">
  <data key="d0">render</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">render is a method in HruleWidget that constructs an Hr Tag and originally mixed the abstraction of rule size with Hr Tag syntax.&lt;SEP&gt;A PathParser method called in doRename to produce the returned path string.&lt;SEP&gt;render is a method called with pageData, also shown as render(true) or render(boolean isSuite), and is described as easier to understand with one input argument or as problematic when using a flag argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="hrSize">
  <data key="d0">hrSize</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">hrSize is a private method that computes the Hr Tag size from a height value representing extra dashes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="extraDashes">
  <data key="d0">extraDashes</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">extraDashes is a field that stores the number of extra dashes used to determine the Hr Tag size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HtmlTag">
  <data key="d0">HtmlTag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HtmlTag is a module that handles HTML tag syntax and was used to separate Hr Tag construction from low-level markup details.&lt;SEP&gt;HtmlTag is a module that was changed long ago to produce markup that conforms to XHTML.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hr Tag">
  <data key="d0">Hr Tag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Hr Tag is an HTML tag that draws a horizontal rule and has a size attribute related to the number of extra dashes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XHTML">
  <data key="d0">XHTML</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">XHTML is a markup standard that requires proper closing syntax for HR tags, such as a self-closing slash.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Size">
  <data key="d0">Size</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Size is the original field or variable in the HruleWidget render code that specified the height of a horizontal rule and was later renamed to extraDashes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Levels Of Abstraction">
  <data key="d0">Levels Of Abstraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Levels Of Abstraction are the different conceptual layers in code, such as the idea that a horizontal rule has a size and the syntax of an HR tag.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Convention">
  <data key="d0">Convention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Convention is a consistently used code structure that others are expected to use and preserve.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AliasWidget">
  <data key="d0">AliasWidget</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AliasWidget is a class mentioned in the prose as a possible containing scope for VariableExpandingWidgetRoot.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FIT">
  <data key="d0">FIT</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">FIT is the software source referenced for the boundary-condition example that uses Parse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tag">
  <data key="d0">Tag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tag is a module that handles the syntactic details involved in generating or processing tags.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HR Tag">
  <data key="d0">HR Tag</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HR Tag is an HTML element represented in code, whose XHTML-conformant form includes a closing slash.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XHTML Standard">
  <data key="d0">XHTML Standard</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">XHTML Standard is a markup standard that requires certain tags, including the HR Tag, to include closing slashes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Separating Levels of Abstraction">
  <data key="d0">Separating Levels of Abstraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Separating Levels of Abstraction is a refactoring concern described as important and difficult to do well.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HruleWidget.render">
  <data key="d0">HruleWidget.render</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">HruleWidget.render is a method whose first refactoring attempt separated abstraction levels but still mixed HR tag construction with size-variable formatting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Size Variable">
  <data key="d0">Size Variable</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Size Variable is a value in HruleWidget.render that is interpreted and formatted to set an HTML size attribute.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G35 Keep Configurable Data at High Levels">
  <data key="d0">G35 Keep Configurable Data at High Levels</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G35 Keep Configurable Data at High Levels is a guideline that configurable constants known at a high level should be passed down rather than buried in low-level functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command-Line Arguments">
  <data key="d0">Command-Line Arguments</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Command-Line Arguments are input values parsed at the start of FitNesse and represented by the Arguments class.&lt;SEP&gt;Command-Line Arguments are the array of strings passed into the main function and supplied to the Args parser.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598260</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DEFAULT_PATH">
  <data key="d0">DEFAULT_PATH</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DEFAULT_PATH is a default configuration constant in Arguments with the value ".".</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DEFAULT_ROOT">
  <data key="d0">DEFAULT_ROOT</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DEFAULT_ROOT is a default configuration constant in Arguments with the value "FitNesseRoot".</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DEFAULT_PORT">
  <data key="d0">DEFAULT_PORT</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DEFAULT_PORT is a default configuration constant in Arguments with the value 80.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DEFAULT_VERSION_DAYS">
  <data key="d0">DEFAULT_VERSION_DAYS</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DEFAULT_VERSION_DAYS is a default configuration constant in Arguments with the value 14.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="G36 Avoid Transitive Navigation">
  <data key="d0">G36 Avoid Transitive Navigation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">G36 Avoid Transitive Navigation is a guideline that modules should know only immediate collaborators and avoid navigation chains through multiple objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pragmatic Programmers">
  <data key="d0">Pragmatic Programmers</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Pragmatic Programmers is a referenced work that calls the transitive-navigation guideline Writing Shy Code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Writing Shy Code">
  <data key="d0">Writing Shy Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Writing Shy Code is a term used by Pragmatic Programmers for modules knowing only immediate collaborators.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="J1 Avoid Long Import Lists by Using Wildcards">
  <data key="d0">J1 Avoid Long Import Lists by Using Wildcards</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">J1 Avoid Long Import Lists by Using Wildcards is a Java guideline that if two or more classes from a package are used, the whole package should be imported with wildcards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="J2 Don't Inherit Constants">
  <data key="d0">J2 Don't Inherit Constants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">J2 Don't Inherit Constants is a Java guideline criticizing the practice of accessing constants by inheriting an interface that defines them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PayrollConstants">
  <data key="d0">PayrollConstants</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PayrollConstants is a Java interface that defines payroll-related constants, including TENTHS_PER_WEEK and OVERTIME_RATE, and is implemented by Employee.&lt;SEP&gt;PayrollConstants is an interface that defines payroll constants TENTHS_PER_WEEK and OVERTIME_RATE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TENTHS_PER_WEEK">
  <data key="d0">TENTHS_PER_WEEK</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">TENTHS_PER_WEEK is a constant integer value set to 400 in PayrollConstants, representing the standard weekly workload in tenths.&lt;SEP&gt;TENTHS_PER_WEEK is a constant in PayrollConstants with the value 400, representing work time in tenths.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Closing Slash">
  <data key="d0">Closing Slash</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Closing Slash is a syntax marker in markup, and the XHTML Standard requires the Closing Slash on the HR Tag.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mixed Levels of Abstraction">
  <data key="d0">Mixed Levels of Abstraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixed Levels of Abstraction is a condition in which a function combines different abstraction levels, such as constructing the HR Tag and formatting the Size Variable in HruleWidget.render.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New Lines of Abstraction">
  <data key="d0">New Lines of Abstraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New Lines of Abstraction are separation points that become visible when a function is broken along existing abstraction lines, as in HruleWidget.render.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configurable Data">
  <data key="d0">Configurable Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Configurable Data includes default values and configuration values that are known and expected at a high level of abstraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration Constants">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Constants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuration Constants are constants such as DEFAULT_PATH, DEFAULT_ROOT, DEFAULT_PORT, and DEFAULT_VERSION_DAYS that configure application behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High-Level Function">
  <data key="d0">High-Level Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High-Level Function is a function at a high level of abstraction that should receive Configurable Data as arguments rather than burying Configurable Data in lower levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low-Level Function">
  <data key="d0">Low-Level Function</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low-Level Function is a function at a lower level of abstraction that should not own or hide Configurable Data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Object Graph">
  <data key="d0">Object Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Object Graph is the network of objects and references in a system that modules might navigate through.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Immediate Collaborators">
  <data key="d0">Immediate Collaborators</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Immediate Collaborators are the direct collaborators with which a module should work and from which the module should request services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Architecture is the overall design and structure of a system; the Architecture can become rigid when too many modules know too much about the Architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;The structural organization of a system or code base.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606382</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A">
  <data key="d0">A</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A is a module that collaborates with B and appears in the transitive-navigation example for G36 Avoid Transitive Navigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="B">
  <data key="d0">B</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">B is a module that collaborates with C and provides navigation from A in the transitive-navigation example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Q">
  <data key="d0">Q</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Q is a module or object that can be interposed between B and C to avoid direct transitive navigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0af28655754ee82c5f5f3411cf8f5c39-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-17.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596259</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wildcards">
  <data key="d0">Wildcards</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Wildcards are Java import syntax symbols used to import a whole package when multiple classes from that package are used.</data>
