<node id="JCommon">
  <data key="d0">JCommon</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">JCommon is a free, open-source general-purpose class library and software framework for the Java platform. It is copyrighted from 2000 to 2005 by Object Refinery Limited and contributors, and it is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License. Project information for JCommon is associated with the jfree.org website, including pages such as http://www.jfree.org/jcommon/index.html and http://www.jfree.org/jcommon/index.php.

JCommon includes date-related functionality, notably the org.jfree.date package and classes such as DayDate. Its name also appears in source headers, including those of DayDate.java and RelativeDayOfWeekRule.java. The JCommon unit tests validate changes made to classes such as SerialDate.

In development contexts, JCommon is described as a framework in which date-related code is being refactored, and certain tables have been reported as unused. Overall, JCommon provides shared general-purpose and date-related utility classes for Java applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598975</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="org.jfree.date">
  <data key="d0">org.jfree.date</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">org.jfree.date is a Java package identifier within the JCommon library that serves as the declared namespace for date-related classes, constants, and utility components. It contains or declares the SerialDate class, the MonthConstants class and MonthConstants.java, and related date/time types such as SpreadsheetDate, DayDate, Month, DateUtil, DateInterval, Day, WeekInMonth, WeekdayRange, DayDateFactory, SpreadsheetDateFactory, and RelativeDayOfWeekRule. Several of these components, including Day, DateInterval, and WeekInMonth, are identified as enum classes.

The package is used in source and test files as the package declaration or import namespace for these components. For example, SerialDateTests.java imports SerialDate and MonthConstants from org.jfree.date, while SpreadsheetDate.java, DayDate.java, and other input source files declare it as their package. Overall, org.jfree.date groups JCommon’s serial-date, calendar, month, weekday, and date-factory functionality under a single Java package.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599089</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="David Gilbert">
  <data key="d0">David Gilbert</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">David Gilbert is an experienced and competent programmer identified as the original author of several Java date-related classes and associated test files, primarily for Object Refinery Limited. He is credited as the author of SerialDate and SerialDate.java, as well as SerialDateTests.java, and is listed in change histories for multiple revisions and bug fixes to date-related classes. According to the descriptions, Gilbert offered the SerialDate code to the community for free and invited public usage and scrutiny.

He is also identified in source code, Java comment headers, and Javadoc documentation as the original author of MonthConstants.java, SpreadsheetDate, SpreadsheetDate.java, RelativeDayOfWeekRule.java, and DayDate. For SpreadsheetDate.java in particular, he is credited with making listed changes to the file, including version creation, method additions, bug fixes, and interface implementation. The descriptions collectively portray David Gilbert as a central contributor to the development and maintenance of these date and time utility classes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="java.util.Date">
  <data key="d0">java.util.Date</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">java.util.Date is a date-related class in Java mentioned as an existing class when considering the purpose of SerialDate.&lt;SEP&gt;java.util.Date is a standard Java date type mentioned as the target type for conversion from DayDate.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java date type returned by the SerialDate toDate method and noted as having more precision than SerialDate.&lt;SEP&gt;java.util.Date is the Java date type returned by the toDate method as an equivalent representation of the SpreadsheetDate.&lt;SEP&gt;java.util.Date is a Java date class imported by SpreadsheetDate.java.&lt;SEP&gt;java.util.Date is a standard Java date class discussed as representing an instant in time too precisely for use when only a particular day is needed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-039</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
