</node>
<node id="testWeekdayCodeToString">
  <data key="d0">testWeekdayCodeToString</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">testWeekdayCodeToString is a test method referenced in the unit tests; the method should not be case sensitive, and using equalsIgnoreCase makes the related behavior pass.&lt;SEP&gt;A test method in SerialDateTest.java that verifies conversion of a Saturday weekday code to the string "Saturday".&lt;SEP&gt;testWeekdayCodeToString is a test method that asserts weekdayCodeToString maps weekday constants to full weekday name strings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="stringToMonthCode">
  <data key="d0">stringToMonthCode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">stringToMonthCode is a function associated with SerialDate that is modified to compare month names case-insensitively and to support additional unit tests.&lt;SEP&gt;stringToMonthCode is a parsing function that converts a string to a month code, is renamed, moved into the Month enum, and simplified.&lt;SEP&gt;A method originally present around lines 428-472 that is renamed, moved into the Month enum, and simplified during refactoring.&lt;SEP&gt;stringToMonthCode is a static method in SerialDate.Java that converts a string to a month code by parsing an integer, a short month name, or a long month name, returning -1 when parsing fails.&lt;SEP&gt;A conversion method that parses a string numeric month representation into a month code constant and returns -1 for invalid string input Hello.&lt;SEP&gt;stringToMonthCode is a function called in the test code that converts a month string representation to a month code, as shown by commented assertions for abbreviated and full month names.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getFollowingDayOfWeek">
  <data key="d0">getFollowingDayOfWeek</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getFollowingDayOfWeek is primarily documented as a method of SerialDate that determines the next occurrence of a specified day of the week after a given date. It is described as a static SerialDate day-of-week calculation method that returns the earliest date after the base date, or after the current SerialDate, that falls on the requested weekday. The change history notes that this SerialDate method was changed to correct bugs in a 2001 update.

The SerialDate implementation is also associated with a known defect located at line 672. Although the method is intended to return the following occurrence of a target weekday, it incorrectly returns the base date when that date already matches the target weekday. This bug was exposed by a commented test concerning the following Saturday after December 25, 2004.

A separate description identifies getFollowingDayOfWeek as a DayDate method that returns a date created by addDays. This appears to refer to a distinct same-named method rather than to the SerialDate implementation, with its behavior described only as generating a date through addDays.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
