<node id="getNearestDayOfWeek">
  <data key="d0">getNearestDayOfWeek</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getNearestDayOfWeek is a day-of-week calculation method most consistently described as a method of SerialDate. Its purpose is to determine the date closest to a given base date that falls on a specified day of the week. In most accounts it is a static method that takes a day-of-week code and a date argument, and returns the nearest matching date. For an invalid day-of-week code, it is expected to throw an IllegalArgumentException. The method is also referenced in testing contexts, including BobsSerialDateTest.java, where it is invoked to verify nearest-occurrence behavior.

According to the change history, getNearestDayOfWeek was changed to correct bugs in a 2001 update. An earlier implementation had a defect in which it failed when the nearest target weekday was in the future. One description further characterizes it as a DayDate method returning a date created by addDays, which may reflect a class-name discrepancy or an implementation detail tied to addDays-based date calculation rather than the predominant SerialDate attribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-031</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
