<node id="IllegalArgumentException">
  <data key="d0">IllegalArgumentException</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IllegalArgumentException is a Java runtime exception class used to signal invalid arguments in date- and time-related utility methods. Rather than returning an error string, it is the recommended failure signal for methods such as weekInMonthToString and relativeToString.

It is thrown or expected in several validation contexts. Month.make, Month.parse, and Month.fromInt throw it when a supplied month index or month code is invalid or does not correspond to a Month enumerator, and Month Code To Quarter may also throw it for an invalid month code. Day methods, including Day.make, Day.parse, and Day.fromInt, throw it when an invalid day index or weekday string is supplied. SerialDate.Java methods throw it when arguments such as a month code or day-of-week code are outside their valid range, including SerialDate weekday methods that receive an invalid day-of-the-week code.

Tests commonly expect or catch IllegalArgumentException to verify that invalid month codes supplied to conversion methods, invalid day-of-week code values, and invalid input to getNearestDayOfWeek produce errors. SpreadsheetDate constructors throw it when the day, month, year, or serial argument is outside the allowed or supported spreadsheet date range, including a serial value beyond the supported range. RelativeDayOfWeekRule.getDate throws it when the supplied year is outside the supported year range.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
