<node id="addDays">
  <data key="d0">addDays</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DayDate method that creates a date by calling createInstance.&lt;SEP&gt;addDays is a SerialDate method that adds a number of days to a base date; the corrected nearest-day-of-week algorithm returns SerialDate.addDays(adjust, base).&lt;SEP&gt;A DayDate method that adds days by converting to an ordinal and constructing a new DayDate, but its name is later considered ambiguous.&lt;SEP&gt;addDays is a static method in SerialDate that creates a new date by adding a possibly negative number of days to a base SerialDate value.&lt;SEP&gt;addDays is a static SerialDate method used to produce a date adjusted from a base date by a day offset.&lt;SEP&gt;A method tested to return a new date after adding a specified number of days to an existing date.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-028</data>
