<node id="Microsoft Excel">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Excel</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft Excel is referenced as the software whose date representation helps explain why the earliest date ordinal is 2 instead of 0.&lt;SEP&gt;Microsoft Excel is a spreadsheet application whose date implementation is used as a comparison for SpreadsheetDate.java and is noted to contain a deliberate bug that treats the year 1900 as a leap year.&lt;SEP&gt;A software product referenced as having a date implementation and a deliberate 1900 leap-year bug.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SpreadsheetDate">
  <data key="d0">SpreadsheetDate</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">SpreadsheetDate is a public Java class in the JCommon library's org.jfree.date package that represents a calendar date using an integer ordinal or serial-number convention in which 1-Jan-1900 equals 2. It supports dates from 1-Jan-1900 through 31-Dec-9999 and, as represented in source listings, constructs date objects that store a date value as a serial or ordinal day, optionally with a description. It provides accessors for year, month, day of month, and day of week, and methods for ordinal-day retrieval, equality, hashing, comparison, static creation from a Java Date, and invocation of calcDayMonthYear, giving a concrete view of ordinal date representation and spreadsheet date handling.

In the described codebase, SpreadsheetDate is presented as a derivative and concrete DayDate implementation created by createInstance, although some descriptions identify it as a concrete subclass of SerialDate, whose factory methods construct SpreadsheetDate instances from date components, a serial number, or a Java Date. This discrepancy may reflect a version, refactoring, or source inconsistency. SpreadsheetDate is also constructed by SpreadsheetDateFactory._makeDate and by the d helper method in date-calculation tests, and it can be instantiated with day, month, and year values obtained from a Calendar instance.

The class contains the original date algorithms and uses date tables. It defines MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED and MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED, and it is referenced as the target for moving EARLIEST_DATE_ORDINAL, LATEST_DATE_ORDINAL, and year-support constants, with these constants also referenced in SpreadsheetDateFactory. Two of its methods call leapYearCount, making leapYearCount a candidate to be pushed down from DayDate, while its ToDate implementation was examined because it does not depend on SpreadsheetDate-specific behavior. It implements getDayOfWeekForOrdinalZero to return Day.SATURDAY.

SpreadsheetDate was also subject to maintenance work: its algorithms were cleaned up, with the final result presented in Listing B-7 through Listing B-16. A 2001 change history records a bug fix, and David Gilbert fixed a bug in SpreadsheetDate on 05-Dec-2001 according to the SerialDate change history.&lt;SEP&gt;SpreadsheetDate is a Java class in which a bug was fixed according to the change log.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-04.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
