</node>
<node id="RelativeDayOfWeekRule">
  <data key="d0">RelativeDayOfWeekRule</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Class that uses MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED and MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED inside the getDate function to validate a year argument.&lt;SEP&gt;RelativeDayOfWeekRule is a Java class in the org.jfree.date package that extends AnnualDateRule and implements an annual date rule based on a reference rule, a day of the week, and a selection parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java class that represents a relative day-of-week date rule and generates a date for a specified year using a sub-rule, a day-of-week value, and a relative attribute.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EARLIEST_DATE_ORDINAL">
  <data key="d0">EARLIEST_DATE_ORDINAL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Date ordinal constant that is used only within SpreadsheetDate and is proposed to be moved from DayDate to SpreadsheetDate.&lt;SEP&gt;A SpreadsheetDate constant with value 2 representing 1/1/1900.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LATEST_DATE_ORDINAL">
  <data key="d0">LATEST_DATE_ORDINAL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Date ordinal constant that is used only within SpreadsheetDate and is proposed to be moved from DayDate to SpreadsheetDate.&lt;SEP&gt;A SpreadsheetDate constant with value 2958465 representing 12/31/9999.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED">
  <data key="d0">MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Year-bound constant associated with DayDate and used by RelativeDayOfWeekRule's getDate function to validate supported years.&lt;SEP&gt;MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED is a constant stored in SpreadsheetDate that defines the minimum year supported by the date implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;A SpreadsheetDate constant with value 1900 indicating the minimum supported year.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED">
  <data key="d0">MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Year-bound constant associated with DayDate and used by RelativeDayOfWeekRule's getDate function to validate supported years.&lt;SEP&gt;MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED is a constant stored in SpreadsheetDate that defines the maximum year supported by the date implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;A SpreadsheetDate constant with value 9999 indicating the maximum supported year.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getDate">
  <data key="d0">getDate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Function in RelativeDayOfWeekRule that validates a year using supported minimum and maximum year values and returns a DayDate instance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="createInstance">
  <data key="d0">createInstance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">DayDate method that creates a SpreadsheetDate instance and is later replaced by makeDate methods in DayDateFactory.&lt;SEP&gt;createInstance is a SerialDate method invoked to construct a new SerialDate value from a serial day number or from day, month, and year components.&lt;SEP&gt;createInstance is a static SerialDate method used to create a date instance from day, month, and year values.&lt;SEP&gt;createInstance is a factory method used to create SerialDate instances from day/month/year arguments or from a serial number argument.&lt;SEP&gt;createInstance is a static SpreadsheetDate factory method that creates a DayDate from a Date using GregorianCalendar, Calendar fields, and Month conversion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599015</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DayDateFactory">
  <data key="d0">DayDateFactory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Abstract factory class introduced to create DayDate instances and answer implementation questions such as minimum and maximum years without making the base class depend on derivatives.&lt;SEP&gt;A factory class invoked by DayDate methods through makeDate to construct new DayDate instances.&lt;SEP&gt;A factory used by GetEndOfMonth to create a DayDate through MakeDate.&lt;SEP&gt;DayDateFactory is a factory class used by DayDate methods to create DayDate instances, including through makeDate calls.&lt;SEP&gt;DayDateFactory is a Java factory class referenced by DayDate.getEndOfMonth for constructing a DayDate through DayDateFactory.makeDate.&lt;SEP&gt;An abstract Java class named DayDateFactory in the org.jfree.date package that maintains a static DayDateFactory factory field initialized to SpreadsheetDateFactory and exposes static makeDate, setInstance, getMinimumYear, and getMaximumYear methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SpreadsheetDateFactory">
  <data key="d0">SpreadsheetDateFactory</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Concrete DayDateFactory subclass that creates SpreadsheetDate instances and is the default factory instance.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java class named SpreadsheetDateFactory in the org.jfree.date package that extends DayDateFactory and implements _makeDate to return SpreadsheetDate objects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Singleton">
  <data key="d0">Singleton</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Pattern noted as part of the combination used by DayDateFactory static methods that delegate to abstract methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="makeDate">
  <data key="d0">makeDate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Static factory method group in DayDateFactory that replaces createInstance and delegates to _makeDate.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of overloaded static methods in DayDateFactory that accept ordinal, day/month/year, or java.util.Date arguments and return DayDate objects by calling factory._makeDate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="_makeDate">
  <data key="d0">_makeDate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Abstract factory method in DayDateFactory that creates DayDate instances and is implemented by SpreadsheetDateFactory.&lt;SEP&gt;_makeDate is a set of overloaded factory methods in DayDate that create SpreadsheetDate instances from day, month, and year arguments or from a Date instance.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of overloaded abstract and concrete methods named _makeDate in DayDateFactory and SpreadsheetDateFactory that produce DayDate or SpreadsheetDate objects from ordinal, day/month/year, or java.util.Date inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="_getMinimumYear">
  <data key="d0">_getMinimumYear</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Abstract method in DayDateFactory that returns the minimum supported year through the selected factory.&lt;SEP&gt;_getMinimumYear is a protected method that returns SpreadsheetDate.MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED.&lt;SEP&gt;A protected method shown in the input snippet that returns SpreadsheetDate.MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED.&lt;SEP&gt;A protected abstract method declared in DayDateFactory and a concrete method implemented in SpreadsheetDateFactory that returns the minimum supported year, using SpreadsheetDate.MINIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED in SpreadsheetDateFactory.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="_getMaximumYear">
  <data key="d0">_getMaximumYear</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Abstract method in DayDateFactory that returns the maximum supported year through the selected factory.&lt;SEP&gt;_getMaximumYear is a protected method that returns SpreadsheetDate.MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED.&lt;SEP&gt;A protected method shown in the input snippet that returns SpreadsheetDate.MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED.&lt;SEP&gt;A protected abstract method declared in DayDateFactory and a concrete method implemented in SpreadsheetDateFactory that returns the maximum supported year, using SpreadsheetDate.MAXIMUM_YEAR_SUPPORTED in SpreadsheetDateFactory.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="setInstance">
  <data key="d0">setInstance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Static method in DayDateFactory that allows replacing the factory instance with a different DayDateFactory.&lt;SEP&gt;A static method in DayDateFactory that assigns a supplied DayDateFactory argument to the static factory field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GregorianCalendar">
  <data key="d0">GregorianCalendar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calendar implementation used in SpreadsheetDateFactory to extract date fields from a java.util.Date.&lt;SEP&gt;GregorianCalendar is a calendar object used to extract day, month, and year fields from a Date instance.&lt;SEP&gt;GregorianCalendar is a Java class imported by SerialDate in the source code.&lt;SEP&gt;GregorianCalendar is a Java calendar class instantiated in the Java Date overload of Create Instance to extract date components from a Java Date.&lt;SEP&gt;GregorianCalendar is a Java calendar class used in the BobsSerialDateTest code to obtain Date objects for 1900 and 2006 during tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java calendar class used in SpreadsheetDateFactory to store a Date and provide Calendar field values for SpreadsheetDate construction.&lt;SEP&gt;GregorianCalendar is a Java calendar class instantiated in SpreadsheetDate createInstance and used to read date parts from a Date value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serial ID">
  <data key="d0">Serial ID</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identifier involved in serialized dates where manual control is argued to avoid invalidating old serialized data, while forgetting to update the identifier can cause undefined or silent failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deserialization">
  <data key="d0">Deserialization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Process of restoring serialized dates across versions, which is described as not to be expected to succeed reliably.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Control">
  <data key="d0">Manual Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Practice of explicitly controlling serial IDs so minor changes do not invalidate previously serialized dates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Old Serialized Dates">
  <data key="d0">Old Serialized Dates</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Previously serialized date data that may become invalid when software changes alter serial IDs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Undefined Failure Mode">
  <data key="d0">Undefined Failure Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failure state caused when an author forgets to update a serial ID, leaving the failure behavior unspecified.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Silent Failure">
  <data key="d0">Silent Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failure state that may occur without a clear error when a serial ID is not updated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
