<node id="Calendar">
  <data key="d0">Calendar</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calendar is a Java date-time utility class, corresponding to java.util.Calendar, that provides date and time field identifiers and constants for date-processing components. Its DATE, MONTH, and YEAR constants are used as field identifiers to obtain date components from a GregorianCalendar instance. These constants are referenced in SpreadsheetDateFactory._makeDate and SpreadsheetDate.createInstance to retrieve date, month, and year values and to construct a SpreadsheetDate instance.

Calendar also supplies day-of-week or weekday constants that SerialDate uses to define equivalent day constants and that are used to initialize the index values of Day enumeration constants. In date-conversion logic, Calendar is instantiated and configured in methods such as DayDate.toDate or a toDate method to produce a Date object from year, month, and day values. Overall, Calendar functions as a shared Java calendar constants and utility type for accessing, mapping, and building date and weekday information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599097</data>
