<node id="LAST_DAY_OF_MONTH">
  <data key="d0">LAST_DAY_OF_MONTH</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">LAST_DAY_OF_MONTH is a table describing the last day of each month, whose descriptive comment is considered redundant because the name is sufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;An array used by lastDayOfMonth that is moved into the Month enum because it belongs with month data.&lt;SEP&gt;LAST_DAY_OF_MONTH is a static integer array in SerialDate storing the number of days in each month in non-leap years.&lt;SEP&gt;LAST_DAY_OF_MONTH is a month-indexed constant or array used by lastDayOfMonth to obtain the default last day of a month before applying any leap-year adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="lastDayOfMonth">
  <data key="d0">lastDayOfMonth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">lastDayOfMonth is a static date-utility method that computes the final day of a specified month and year, returning the last valid day number for that month. It is described in related contexts as a method in SerialDate and as a static method in DateUtil, with one description indicating that it was moved from DayDate into DateUtil. This suggests that the function may have been refactored between classes while retaining the same core behavior.

The method determines the result by handling February explicitly, using Month.lastDay, Month.FEBRUARY, and isLeapYear. It returns month.lastDay() plus one when the month is February and the year is a leap year; otherwise, it returns month.lastDay(). It is used to establish the last valid day of a month, to validate that a supplied day argument does not exceed the final day for the specified month and year, and it is covered by tests that verify correct final-day behavior, including leap-year February.

lastDayOfMonth also provides the same data as the LAST_DAY_OF_MONTH table and is associated with supporting the ability to make that table private.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH">
  <data key="d0">AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH is a table of aggregate days to the end of the month that is reported as unused anywhere in the JCommon framework and therefore deleted.&lt;SEP&gt;AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH is a static integer array in SerialDate storing the number of days in a non-leap year up to the end of each month.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LEAP_YEAR_AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH">
  <data key="d0">LEAP_YEAR_AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">LEAP_YEAR_AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH is a leap-year counterpart table to AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH that is likewise deleted as unnecessary.&lt;SEP&gt;LEAP_YEAR_AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_MONTH is a static integer array in SerialDate storing the number of days in a leap year up to the end of each month.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
