<node id="AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_PRECEDING_MONTH">
  <data key="d0">AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_PRECEDING_MONTH</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_PRECEDING_MONTH is a table of aggregate days to the end of the preceding month that is used only in SpreadsheetDate and considered for moving closer to its use.&lt;SEP&gt;AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_PRECEDING_MONTH is a static integer array in SerialDate storing the number of days in a non-leap year up to the end of the preceding month.&lt;SEP&gt;AGGREGATE_DAYS_TO_END_OF_PRECEDING_MONTH is an aggregate data table in SerialDate that stores the number of days to the end of each preceding month for non-leap year calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WeekInMonth">
  <data key="d0">WeekInMonth</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">WeekInMonth is an enum with FIRST, SECOND, THIRD, FOURTH, and LAST enumerators that replaces constants selecting a week within a month.&lt;SEP&gt;An enum created earlier and used to hold week-in-month values and to provide a ToString-based representation.&lt;SEP&gt;WeekInMonth is a Java enum representing positions within a month, with constants FIRST, SECOND, THIRD, FOURTH, and LAST, and an integer index accessor toInt.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java source type named WeekInMonth that includes constants THIRD(3), FOURTH(4), and LAST(0), a private final int index field, a constructor accepting an integer index, and a toInt method returning the index.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DateInterval">
  <data key="d0">DateInterval</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">DateInterval is an enum with CLOSED, CLOSED_LEFT, CLOSED_RIGHT, and OPEN enumerators that replaces endpoint-inclusion constants using interval nomenclature.&lt;SEP&gt;DateInterval is an enum that replaces a switch statement in isInRange with interval constants and an abstract isIn method.&lt;SEP&gt;DateInterval is a Java enum defining interval boundary semantics OPEN, CLOSED_LEFT, CLOSED_RIGHT, and CLOSED. It declares an abstract boolean method isIn for testing whether a value lies between left and right bounds.&lt;SEP&gt;DateInterval is a Java interval type used by DayDate.isInRange, including the constant DateInterval.CLOSED and the interval.isIn method.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WeekdayRange">
  <data key="d0">WeekdayRange</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">WeekdayRange is an enum with LAST, NEXT, and NEAREST enumerators that replaces constants describing the desired weekday search result.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java enum named WeekdayRange in the org.jfree.date package with constants LAST, NEAREST, and NEXT.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
