  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An original DayDate function for adding a number of years, shown in the refactored code as plusYears.&lt;SEP&gt;addYears is a method of SerialDate whose bug was fixed on 05-Jan-2005 with issue reference 1096282.&lt;SEP&gt;addYears is a static SerialDate method that creates a new date by adding a specified number of years, which can be negative, to a base date.&lt;SEP&gt;A method tested to return a new date after adding one year to existing dates, including leap-year February handling.&lt;SEP&gt;A date adjustment method invoked to add one year to a date value in a test assertion.</data>
