<node id="getMonth">
  <data key="d0">getMonth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getMonth is a method name used in several date-related classes to retrieve the month component associated with a date. Its exact implementation differs by class, but it consistently provides access to the month value, typically represented with January as 1.

In the DayDate class, getMonth is described as an abstract date method and one of the nicely abstract methods available on the class. It returns the Month component of a date and is used by DayDate methods such as addMonths and plusYears.

In the SerialDate class, getMonth is an abstract accessor method invoked on a SerialDate instance or base date to obtain the month number or month value of the year. It returns the month with January represented as 1, February as 2, and March as 3, continuing sequentially through the remaining months.

In the SpreadsheetDate class, getMonth is a public method that returns the Month value held by a SpreadsheetDate instance. Across these contexts, getMonth serves as a shared accessor concept for date-related objects, although it belongs to different classes and may have different signatures and abstractions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599092</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getDayOfMonth">
  <data key="d0">getDayOfMonth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getDayOfMonth is a method name used in multiple date-related classes to retrieve the day-of-month component of a date. Across the provided descriptions, it appears in DayDate, SerialDate, and SpreadsheetDate, where its exact role and visibility differ slightly.

In DayDate, getDayOfMonth is described as an abstract date method and one of the nicely abstract methods. It returns the day-of-month component of a DayDate value and is used to clamp result dates in operations such as addMonths and plusYears.

In SerialDate, getDayOfMonth functions as an accessor method for a base date or SerialDate instance, returning the day of the month. One description identifies it as an abstract SerialDate method, while others describe it as a method invoked on an instance to obtain the day-of-month value, suggesting minor uncertainty about whether the reference is to an abstract declaration or a concrete accessor.

In SpreadsheetDate, getDayOfMonth is a public method that returns the day value held by a SpreadsheetDate object.&lt;SEP&gt;getDayOfMonth is a Java method that returns the dayOfMonth field and is shown with a redundant Javadoc comment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-04.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604159</data>
