  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="compare">
  <data key="d0">compare</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">compare is an original method name for a day-difference operation that is pulled into DayDate and renamed to daysSince because the original name does not communicate the return value.&lt;SEP&gt;An abstract SerialDate method that returns the difference in days between the current date and another SerialDate.&lt;SEP&gt;compare is a method that returns the difference in days between the current SpreadsheetDate and another specified SerialDate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isInRange">
  <data key="d0">isInRange</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">isInRange is a method moved into DayDate and refactored to determine whether a day is inside a range by using DateInterval.&lt;SEP&gt;isInRange is a method of SerialDate whose javadocs were updated on 04-Sep-2003.&lt;SEP&gt;isInRange is an overloaded abstract method of SerialDate that returns a boolean indicating whether a SerialDate falls within a specified range, with one form using inclusive endpoints and another form using an integer inclusion flag.&lt;SEP&gt;isInRange is a public method of SerialDate that returns a boolean indicating whether the SerialDate falls within a specified date range, using an include code to control whether boundary dates are included.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-036</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isIn">
  <data key="d0">isIn</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">isIn is an abstract method defined in DateInterval and implemented by interval constants to test whether an ordinal day lies inside an interval.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="correctLastDayOfMonth">
  <data key="d0">correctLastDayOfMonth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">correctLastDayOfMonth is a newly extracted method that eliminates duplication between plusYears and plusMonths and makes the related methods clearer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790596802</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="toInt">
  <data key="d0">toInt</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">toInt is an accessor created for enums to expose an integer value while the index field is made private.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of WeekInMonth that returns the integer index value associated with the WeekInMonth constant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-042</data>
