<node id="getYYYY">
  <data key="d0">getYYYY</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getYYYY is an abstract date method identified in DayDate as one of the nicely abstract methods.&lt;SEP&gt;getYYYY is a SerialDate accessor method used to obtain the year component of a date.&lt;SEP&gt;An abstract SerialDate method that returns the year, assumed valid from 1900 to 9999.&lt;SEP&gt;getYYYY is a SerialDate accessor method called on a base date to retrieve the four-digit year value.&lt;SEP&gt;getYYYY is a method invoked on a SerialDate instance to obtain the four-digit year value.&lt;SEP&gt;getYYYY is a method that returns the year for the date, assuming a valid range of 1900 to 9999.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-034</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-16.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599015</data>
