</node>
<node id="Math.min">
  <data key="d0">Math.min</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Math.min is a static method used to calculate the left boundary from two ordinal day values in isInRange.&lt;SEP&gt;Math.min is a standard Java method invoked by addMonths to return the smaller of the base day of month and the computed last day of the target month.&lt;SEP&gt;Math.min is a static Java utility method invoked to select the smaller of two numeric values in date calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;Math.min is a Java standard method that returns the smaller of two integer values, and isInRange uses it to determine the start serial value for a date range.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f738bd6b0c75b6d085747dd812187c7e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-036</data>
