<node id="Schema">
  <data key="d0">Schema</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Schema is an alternative term for the format string that defines command-line argument names and types.&lt;SEP&gt;Schema is a private String field declared in the Args class in the first draft, named schema.&lt;SEP&gt;Comma-separated argument description format used by Args to declare Boolean and String argument elements&lt;SEP&gt;Schema is a String instance variable in Args that represents the argument schema and is checked during parsing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014</data>
