<node id="ArgsException.ErrorCode">
  <data key="d0">ArgsException.ErrorCode</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ArgsException.ErrorCode is a nested error-code type inside ArgsException that defines error-code constants referenced by static imports, including MISSING_STRING, MISSING_INTEGER, and INVALID_INTEGER.&lt;SEP&gt;ArgsException.ErrorCode is an error-code namespace used by ArgsException and imported statically in the Args implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;ArgsException.ErrorCode is a nested error-code holder within ArgsException that defines constant values such as MISSING_DOUBLE, INVALID_DOUBLE, UNEXPECTED_ARGUMENT, INVALID_ARGUMENT_NAME, INVALID_FORMAT, MISSING_STRING, INVALID_INTEGER, and MISSING_INTEGER.&lt;SEP&gt;ArgsException.ErrorCode is an enumeration inside ArgsException that lists the possible error conditions supported by the exception, including OK, INVALID_FORMAT, UNEXPECTED_ARGUMENT, INVALID_ARGUMENT_NAME, MISSING_STRING, MISSING_INTEGER, INVALID_INTEGER, MISSING_DOUBLE, and INVALID_DOUBLE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598260</data>
