<node id="BooleanArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d0">BooleanArgumentMarshaler</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">BooleanArgumentMarshaler is a private inner Java class within Args that provides an ArgumentMarshaler implementation for boolean arguments; descriptions refer to it variously as extending or implementing ArgumentMarshaler. It is created or instantiated by Args, including through parseSchemaElement, when a boolean schema element is identified by an empty elementTail, no suffix, or no type tail. In that case, BooleanArgumentMarshaler is inserted into the Args map fields as the concrete marshaler representing the boolean argument value.

Functionally, BooleanArgumentMarshaler stores a boolean value and uses its set behavior, associated with setArgument, to mark that stored value as true when the corresponding argument token is present. It exposes a value accessor—described in one account as a static getValue method and in other accounts as get—that returns the stored boolean result. The class is also identified as the target for moving or forwarding setBooleanArg logic, making it the dedicated marshaler type for suffix-less boolean schema elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="StringArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d0">StringArgumentMarshaler</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">StringArgumentMarshaler is a private inner Java class associated with the Args class that provides argument marshaling for string values. It functions as a concrete ArgumentMarshaler, with descriptions alternatively characterizing it as implementing or extending ArgumentMarshaler. The class is selected or instantiated by Args, including within parseSchemaElement, when a schema element’s tail or elementTail is an asterisk (*), and it is inserted into Args map fields to handle the corresponding string argument.

In operation, StringArgumentMarshaler stores a String value and manages the set and get behavior for that argument. Its set behavior is associated with setArgument and consumes the next token from the associated Iterator; if the required token is absent, it reports a missing string error by throwing ArgsException. Its get behavior returns the stored string value, and it also provides a static getValue method that returns a String result. Overall, StringArgumentMarshaler is the specific marshaler used by Args for string argument schema elements marked with the asterisk suffix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598355</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IntegerArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d0">IntegerArgumentMarshaler</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">IntegerArgumentMarshaler is a Java class representing a specific ArgumentMarshaler implementation used for integer arguments. It is described variously as a private class, private inner class, subclass, or implementation of ArgumentMarshaler, and functions as a concrete ArgumentMarshaler derivative created by Args for schema elements marked with a hash, particularly when the element tail is "#". It stores a parsed integer value, often in an intValue field, and is inserted into Args map fields as the marshaler associated with an integer argument.

During marshaling, IntegerArgumentMarshaler handles set and get operations for integer arguments, including setArgument and corresponding retrieval methods. It parses the next iterator token, an integer string, or an integer value into an int and stores the result. Its get behavior returns the parsed integer value, and it is also described as providing a static getValue method that returns an int result. If the required integer token is absent or cannot be parsed, IntegerArgumentMarshaler reports an ArgsException indicating a missing or invalid integer value.

Overall, IntegerArgumentMarshaler acts as the internal integer-argument marshaler selected for integer schema elements, serving both as a placeholder representing integer argument values and as the concrete mechanism by which Args captures, validates, and returns parsed integer arguments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
