</node>
<node id="Args.java">
  <data key="d0">Args.java</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Args.java is a Java source-file listing that documents the development of the Args command-line argument parser. It presents a first-draft implementation of the Args class, including imports, an argument schema, command-line argument handling, and data structures for boolean, string, and integer arguments. The file contains the parsing methods and typed accessors used to parse command-line input against a declared schema and expose the parsed values in typed form.

Across the referenced listings—14-8, 14-9, 14-10, and 14-12—Args.java represents different stages of the same incremental implementation and refactoring process. The parser initially supports Boolean arguments and is later extended to handle String arguments, while the broader draft also includes structures for integer arguments. The source file is associated with a package under objectmentor, and after the first refactoring it declares the com.objectmentor.utilities.getopts package and contains the Args class with its argument-marshaling methods and inner classes. During this refactoring, the ArgumentMarshaler skeleton is appended to Args.java, making the file a key artifact in the evolution of the argument-parsing design.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
