<node id="parseSchemaElement">
  <data key="d0">parseSchemaElement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">parseSchemaElement is a function mentioned as needing a new case statement when a new argument type is added to the argument parsing program.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method in Args that parses one schema element, validates the leading character, and initializes the corresponding argument type.&lt;SEP&gt;A method that validates a schema element identifier and dispatches it to Boolean or String schema element parsing&lt;SEP&gt;Private Args method that dispatches a single-character schema element to parseBooleanSchemaElement.&lt;SEP&gt;parseSchemaElement is a method in Args that parses a schema element and inserts the corresponding Boolean, String, or Integer ArgumentMarshaler into the marshalers map.&lt;SEP&gt;parseSchemaElement parses a schema element, validates its identifier, and stores the appropriate marshaler in marshalers based on the element tail, throwing ParseException for unsupported tails.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method of Args that validates a schema element identifier and selects the appropriate ArgumentMarshaler based on the element suffix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
