<node id="Teachers">
  <data key="d0">Teachers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Teachers are grade-school educators mentioned as trying to teach students the process of writing rough drafts and refining compositions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freshman Programmers">
  <data key="d0">Freshman Programmers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Freshman Programmers are novice programmers described as focusing primarily on making a program work and often leaving it in a messy state.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seasoned Programmers">
  <data key="d0">Seasoned Programmers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Seasoned Programmers are experienced programmers who recognize that leaving a working program messy is a professional risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getBoolean">
  <data key="d0">getBoolean</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getBoolean is a public accessor method in the Args class that retrieves the Boolean value associated with a specified argument character. It works with the argument storage maintained by Args, which is described in some accounts as booleanArgs and, after a refactoring, as the marshalers map used to resolve argument values.

In operation, getBoolean obtains the entry for the supplied argument character, typically by invoking a get method on booleanArgs or by delegating to BooleanArgumentMarshaler.getValue through the marshaler map, and then casts or extracts the result as a Boolean. If the associated value is absent, null, or handled by falseIfNull, the method returns false. It also returns false when the required marshaler is missing, cannot be cast to the expected type, or a ClassCastException occurs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Set">
  <data key="d0">Set</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Set is a Java collection type used in the Args.java first draft to store unexpected arguments and found arguments as Character elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Set is a method prefix and mutator term prescribed by the Javabean Standard.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Character">
  <data key="d0">Character</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Character is a Java type used in the Args.java first draft as keys for argument maps and sets.&lt;SEP&gt;Java class used by parseBooleanSchemaElement through isLetter to determine whether a schema element is a letter character.&lt;SEP&gt;Character is a Java character wrapper class used as the key type for Args argument storage maps.&lt;SEP&gt;Character is the Java character type used as the key type in the argument marshaler maps in the Args class.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TreeSet">
  <data key="d0">TreeSet</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">TreeSet is a Java sorted-set implementation used in the Args.java first draft for the unexpectedArguments field.&lt;SEP&gt;Java Set implementation used to initialize unexpectedArguments in the Boolean-only Args draft.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
