<node id="schema">
  <data key="d0">schema</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A String field in Args that holds the comma-delimited argument schema.&lt;SEP&gt;String field in Args describing the accepted argument specification.&lt;SEP&gt;String field in Args that stores the argument schema and is used for parsing, validation, and usage generation&lt;SEP&gt;schema is a string schema that describes supported argument characters and is used to generate usage text.&lt;SEP&gt;String field in Args that defines the usage schema and is included in the usage string when nonempty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="args">
  <data key="d0">args</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A String array field in Args that holds input argument strings.&lt;SEP&gt;String array field in Args holding the command-line arguments to be parsed.&lt;SEP&gt;String array field in Args that stores the received command-line arguments&lt;SEP&gt;args is a String[] instance variable in Args representing the original command-line argument values.&lt;SEP&gt;Argument array referenced by Args methods and proposed to be converted into a list for Iterator-based access.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="valid">
  <data key="d0">valid</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A boolean field in Args that records whether parsing succeeded, initialized true and set false on errors.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean field in Args indicating whether argument parsing succeeded.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean field in Args that indicates whether the parsed arguments are valid&lt;SEP&gt;valid is a boolean state that tracks whether the parsed arguments are valid.&lt;SEP&gt;valid is a boolean state set to false when setArgument catches ArgsException, indicating that the argument set is invalid.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean field in Args that indicates whether parsed arguments are valid and is returned by isValid.&lt;SEP&gt;valid is a flag in the argument-processing context set to false when setArgument catches an ArgsException.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598385</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getString">
  <data key="d0">getString</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getString is a public accessor method in Args that retrieves the String value associated with a specified argument character. It obtains the value by looking up the relevant argument marshaler for that character, typically from stringArgs or the marshaler map, and then delegates to StringArgumentMarshaler.getValue or the corresponding ArgumentMarshaler implementation.

The method provides safe read access to string arguments by handling missing or malformed data gracefully. When the stored value is null, it uses blankIfNull, and when no marshaler exists for the character or a ClassCastException occurs while accessing or casting the marshaler, it returns an empty string. These behaviors ensure that getString returns a usable String value rather than propagating an exception for absent or incompatible arguments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="intArgs">
  <data key="d0">intArgs</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Map from Character to Integer in Args that stores integer argument values, initialized zero for integer schema elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Map-like field in Args that stores integer argument values keyed by argument character and is read by the getInt accessor.&lt;SEP&gt;intArgs is a private HashMap field in Args that mapped Character keys to ArgumentMarshaler values for Integer arguments.&lt;SEP&gt;intArgs is a field in Args that stores integer argument marshalers by character key.&lt;SEP&gt;intArgs is a private Map field in Args that stores ArgumentMarshaler instances for integer arguments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="argsFound">
  <data key="d0">argsFound</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A Set of Character in Args that records argument characters encountered while parsing arguments.&lt;SEP&gt;Collection-like field in Args that stores argument characters identified during parsing.&lt;SEP&gt;argsFound is a data collection that records argument characters recognized during parsing.&lt;SEP&gt;Set of Character field in Args declared for tracking discovered argument characters&lt;SEP&gt;Collection in Args that stores found argument characters and is used by cardinality and has.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="unexpectedArguments">
  <data key="d0">unexpectedArguments</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A Set of Character in Args that records argument characters not declared in the schema.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of Character values used to collect argument characters that are not part of the declared schema&lt;SEP&gt;Collection-like field in Args that stores argument characters not expected by the schema.&lt;SEP&gt;unexpectedArguments is a data collection that records argument characters not recognized during parsing.&lt;SEP&gt;Iterable field in Args that stores unexpected argument characters and is processed by unexpectedArgumentMessage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="errorArgumentId">
  <data key="d0">errorArgumentId</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A Character field in Args that stores the argument character associated with a parsing error, initialized null character.&lt;SEP&gt;Character field in Args identifying the argument character associated with an error.&lt;SEP&gt;errorArgumentId is a character field set to the argument character that caused an ArgsException in setArgument.&lt;SEP&gt;Field in Args that stores an argument identifier used in formatted error messages.&lt;SEP&gt;errorArgumentId is a field assigned the current argChar when setArgument catches an ArgsException.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="errorCode">
  <data key="d0">errorCode</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An ErrorCode field in Args that stores the current error state, initialized OK.&lt;SEP&gt;Field in Args that stores the current ErrorCode value used by errorMessage and updated when argument parsing detects an error.&lt;SEP&gt;ErrorCode field in Args initialized to OK and used to record the parse error state&lt;SEP&gt;errorCode is a status value that represents an argument-parsing error condition.&lt;SEP&gt;errorCode is a field holding the current ErrorCode value, assigned to MISSING_INTEGER, INVALID_INTEGER, MISSING_DOUBLE, or INVALID_DOUBLE during parsing.&lt;SEP&gt;Field in Args that holds an ErrorCode value and is set by argument-processing methods or read by errorMessage.&lt;SEP&gt;errorCode is a variable assigned error-code constants when StringArgumentMarshaler or IntegerArgumentMarshaler detects a missing or invalid argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="parseSchema">
  <data key="d0">parseSchema</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that splits schema by commas and parses nonempty trimmed schema elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A method that splits the schema string into comma-separated elements, trims each nonempty element, and delegates it to parseSchemaElement&lt;SEP&gt;Private Args method that iterates over schema elements and delegates to parseSchemaElement for each element.&lt;SEP&gt;parseSchema is a method called by parse to interpret the argument schema before argument parsing.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method of Args that splits the schema string by commas and processes each nonempty schema element.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
