<node id="parseArguments">
  <data key="d0">parseArguments</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that iterates over the args array and parses each argument string.&lt;SEP&gt;A method that iterates over the received argument strings and delegates each argument to parseArgument&lt;SEP&gt;Private Args method that iterates over args and calls parseArgument for each argument string.&lt;SEP&gt;parseArguments is a private method that iterates over an args array and invokes parseArgument for each entry.&lt;SEP&gt;parseArguments is a private method in Args that iterates currentArgument over argsList and calls parseArgument for each argument.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method of Args that iterates over the stored argument list and parses each command-line argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="parseArgument">
  <data key="d0">parseArgument</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that parses an argument string when the string begins with a hyphen.&lt;SEP&gt;A method that checks whether an argument begins with a dash and delegates processing to parseElements&lt;SEP&gt;Private Args method that processes a single argument string by invoking parseElements when the string starts with a dash.&lt;SEP&gt;parseArgument is a private method that checks whether an argument begins with a dash and delegates to parseElements.&lt;SEP&gt;parseArgument is a method invoked by parseArguments to process a single argument string.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method of Args that recognizes argument strings beginning with a hyphen and forwards them for element parsing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="parseElements">
  <data key="d0">parseElements</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that parses each character after the leading hyphen of an argument string.&lt;SEP&gt;A method that iterates over the characters of a dash-prefixed argument string and delegates each character to parseElement&lt;SEP&gt;parseElements is a private method that iterates through characters of an option argument and invokes parseElement for each character.&lt;SEP&gt;Private Args method invoked by parseArgument to process the characters of a dash-prefixed argument string; the listing shows its beginning only.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method of Args that iterates over the characters of a hyphen-prefixed argument string and parses each character.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="parseElement">
  <data key="d0">parseElement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that calls setArgument for an argument character and records unexpected characters and error state when setArgument returns false.&lt;SEP&gt;A method that processes a single argument character by setting a Boolean argument or recording it as unexpected&lt;SEP&gt;parseElement is a private method that attempts to set an argument, records recognized arguments in argsFound, records unrecognized characters in unexpectedArguments, and updates the valid flag.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method of Args that attempts to set an argument value and throws ArgsException when the argument is unexpected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MISSING_INTEGER">
  <data key="d0">MISSING_INTEGER</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">MISSING_INTEGER is an ErrorCode constant in the Args library, specifically an ArgsException.ErrorCode value, that identifies the error condition in which a required integer parameter is absent. It is assigned or asserted when a required integer argument value is not present in the argument iterator or is not supplied in the command-line arguments.

As an error-code value, MISSING_INTEGER indicates that an expected integer parameter was not found for an argument. In practical terms, it represents the missing-integer-argument condition and is used to report that the program could not obtain the required integer value during argument parsing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="setIntArg">
  <data key="d0">setIntArg</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that stores an integer argument value and sets error state when an integer parameter is missing or invalid.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg is a method in Args that sets an integer argument through an ArgumentMarshaler.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg is a private method in Args that reads the next command-line parameter, parses the parameter as an integer, and records an error when parsing fails.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg is a method in Args that sets an integer argument by incrementing currentArgument, calling the marshaler set method with args[currentArgument], setting ErrorCode.MISSING_INTEGER or ErrorCode.INVALID_INTEGER, and throwing or rethrowing ArgsException.&lt;SEP&gt;Method in Args that processes an integer argument by advancing currentArgument, reading args, and setting the provided marshaler.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg is a private method in Args that reads the next value from currentArgument, calls ArgumentMarshaler.set, and sets error state when the value is missing or invalid.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg is a helper method previously used for integer arguments and later replaced by the set method.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MISSING_STRING">
  <data key="d0">MISSING_STRING</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">MISSING_STRING is an ErrorCode constant, specifically an ArgsException.ErrorCode enum value, used in argument parsing contexts to represent a missing required string parameter. It identifies the error state in which a required String argument is absent, not supplied, or cannot be located when the argument iterator or command line arguments are processed.

The constant is assigned or asserted by Args when the expected string value for a required argument is not found. In this way, MISSING_STRING serves as the standard error-code value indicating that a string argument is missing from the provided input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isIntArg">
  <data key="d0">isIntArg</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A private method in Args that checks whether intArgs contains a given argument character.&lt;SEP&gt;isIntArg is a method in Args that identifies integer argument marshalers through marshalers after refactoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OK">
  <data key="d0">OK</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An ErrorCode constant in Args that indicates no parsing error.&lt;SEP&gt;ErrorCode value indicating successful parsing that the errorMessage method treats as an unexpected state.&lt;SEP&gt;Enum constant in ErrorCode indicating the default successful parse error state&lt;SEP&gt;Error code value representing no error, used in errorMessage to trigger an internal TILT exception.&lt;SEP&gt;OK is an ArgsException.ErrorCode value indicating a non-error state, and errorMessage throws a TILT exception when OK is the current error code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="currentArgument">
  <data key="d0">currentArgument</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An int field in Args that tracks the index into the args array while arguments are being parsed.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer field in Args used as the loop index while parsing the args array&lt;SEP&gt;currentArgument is an integer index variable used by setStringArg to locate the current value in the argument values array.&lt;SEP&gt;currentArgument is an Iterator&lt;String&gt; instance variable in Args used to traverse argsList and supply the next argument to set functions.&lt;SEP&gt;currentArgument is an Iterator variable passed to set methods to consume argument tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;Instance variable in Args that tracks the current argument index and is incremented before reading args in setIntArg and setStringArg.&lt;SEP&gt;currentArgument is an Iterator&lt;String&gt; object used as a parameter in set to supply the next argument value for a marshaler.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="errorParameter">
  <data key="d0">errorParameter</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">String field in Args holding an offending parameter value used in error messages.&lt;SEP&gt;A String field in Args that stores the parameter associated with a parsing error and is initialized to TILT.&lt;SEP&gt;errorParameter is a string field set to the failed parameter when an integer or double parameter cannot be parsed.&lt;SEP&gt;String field in Args that stores a parameter involved in an argument error and is used in the invalid integer message.&lt;SEP&gt;errorParameter is a field assigned the current parameter when IntegerArgumentMarshaler catches an ArgsException while parsing an integer argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598402</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="INVALID_INTEGER">
  <data key="d0">INVALID_INTEGER</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">INVALID_INTEGER is an error-code constant defined in the Args library as a value of ArgsException.ErrorCode. It represents an invalid integer parameter and is assigned when a command-line argument or parameter that is expected to be an integer cannot be parsed or converted to an integer value.

The code is used to signal that an integer argument was present but its value was invalid, such as a non-numeric string like "Forty two". In this situation, the Args library reports INVALID_INTEGER to identify the specific parsing or type-conversion failure associated with the integer argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598403</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ParseException">
  <data key="d0">ParseException</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ParseException is a Java exception class associated with the Args component in a first-draft implementation of argument and schema parsing. In that source, it was imported by Args.java and used as the exception type declared or thrown by the Args constructor and by schema parsing methods when parsing failed or schema validation did not succeed.

Specifically, ParseException was reported by Args methods, including parseSchemaElement, when an argument or schema element had an invalid format. The exception thus signified that a supplied schema element or argument could not be parsed correctly. During a later refactoring of the argument parsing design, ParseException was removed from the design, indicating that it was part of the earlier implementation rather than the revised approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isBooleanArg">
  <data key="d0">isBooleanArg</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Private Args method that reports whether booleanArgs contains a supplied argument character.&lt;SEP&gt;A private method in Args that is called by setArgument to determine whether an argument character is a declared boolean argument.&lt;SEP&gt;isBooleanArg is a method in Args that identifies boolean argument marshalers, initially through booleanArgs and later through marshalers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ErrorCode">
  <data key="d0">ErrorCode</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ErrorCode is a name used for closely related enumerations or constant groups that represent argument-parsing error states. The provided descriptions can be divided into two contexts: an Args context and an ArgsException context. The overlap in their constants suggests that they may represent the same conceptual error taxonomy associated with argument parsing, or two distinct nested types that share the same name.

In the Args context, ErrorCode is described as a private enum, code type, error-code structure, or container for error-code constants defined inside Args. It is used by Args to record and classify argument validation errors, such as missing or invalid values, and to track parsing error states. Its listed values include OK, MISSING_STRING, MISSING_INTEGER, INVALID_INTEGER, and UNEXPECTED_ARGUMENT, with some descriptions also including MISSING_DOUBLE and INVALID_DOUBLE. It is assigned during argument processing to capture specific failure reasons, including a missing string or invalid numeric value.

In the ArgsException context, ErrorCode is described as an enum nested inside ArgsException. It represents argument parsing error states and is used to record specific failure reasons, including MISSING_STRING during string argument processing. Its values are reported to include OK, INVALID_ARGUMENT_FORMAT, also described in one description as INVALID_FORMAT, UNEXPECTED_ARGUMENT, INVALID_ARGUMENT_NAME, and missing or invalid numeric codes such as MISSING_STRING, MISSING_INTEGER, INVALID_INTEGER, MISSING_DOUBLE, and INVALID_DOUBLE. The descriptions do not conclusively establish whether the Args and ArgsException references denote the same enumeration or separate enumerations with identical names.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
