  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method that returns an error message constructed from unexpectedArguments or an empty string when no unexpected arguments are present&lt;SEP&gt;Public Args method that returns a formatted error message based on errorCode and error details.&lt;SEP&gt;errorMessage is a public method that constructs an error message from unexpectedArguments or an error code.&lt;SEP&gt;Method in Args that returns an error message selected by errorCode, including messages for unexpected, missing, and invalid arguments.&lt;SEP&gt;errorMessage returns a formatted error message based on the current errorCode, with messages for unexpected arguments, missing strings, invalid integers, and missing integers.&lt;SEP&gt;A method of ArgsException that formats error messages based on error parameters, highlighted in the text as a design concern related to SRP.&lt;SEP&gt;errorMessage is the method of ArgsException and is associated with error message formatting.</data>
