  <data key="d0">String Argument Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">String Argument Type is an argument type for string values that requires schema parsing, command-line conversion, and a getter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integer Argument Type">
  <data key="d0">Integer Argument Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Integer Argument Type is an argument type whose addition caused the argument-parsing code to become less maintainable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boolean Argument Type">
  <data key="d0">Boolean Argument Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Boolean Argument Type is an argument type for boolean values supported by Args.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Argument Type">
  <data key="d0">Argument Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Argument Type is a general category of command-line argument types that require schema parsing, command-line conversion, and typed accessors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Command-Line Strings">
  <data key="d0">Command-Line Strings</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Command-Line Strings are input strings from which argument characters are parsed and converted to typed values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getXXX Method">
  <data key="d0">getXXX Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getXXX Method is a pattern of typed accessor methods that return argument values to callers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598413</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="stringArgs">
  <data key="d0">stringArgs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">stringArgs is a map-like field in the Args class used to associate string arguments with their character-based keys. In one reported form, it is a private map or HashMap from Character to String that stores declared or parsed string argument values. Under this interpretation, each argument character maps to a string value, and the collection may be initialized with an empty string for string schema elements. This version of stringArgs functions as direct storage for the values supplied for string-typed arguments.

Other descriptions identify stringArgs as a private map field in Args that stores ArgumentMarshaler instances for string arguments, using Character keys to retrieve the corresponding marshalers. In this variant, the field does not directly hold raw string values but instead holds objects responsible for processing or marshaling string arguments. These descriptions may reflect different implementations, versions, or abstraction levels of the same Args field. Overall, stringArgs is best understood as a Character-keyed data collection in Args used for handling string arguments, either by storing their parsed values or by storing the marshalers associated with those arguments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Listing 14-11">
  <data key="d0">Listing 14-11</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Listing 14-11 is a code listing that shows the ArgumentMarshaler class and its marshaler subclasses appended to Args.java.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="setBoolean">
  <data key="d0">setBoolean</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">setBoolean is a method of ArgumentMarshaler that assigns a supplied boolean value to the marshaler's stored boolean value.&lt;SEP&gt;setBoolean is a method originally defined in ArgumentMarshaler that assigns a boolean value to booleanValue before being removed after set deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="setString">
  <data key="d0">setString</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">setString is a method of ArgumentMarshaler that stores a supplied string value for a string argument.&lt;SEP&gt;setString is a method in ArgumentMarshaler that assigns a supplied String value to the stringValue field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="StringArgumentMarshaller">
  <data key="d0">StringArgumentMarshaller</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">StringArgumentMarshaller is an ArgumentMarshaler derivative for string arguments that is expected to use the String parameter supplied to the abstract set method.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing String">
  <data key="d0">Missing String</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Missing String is an ErrorCode value assigned when a string argument is absent from the command line.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing Integer">
  <data key="d0">Missing Integer</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Missing Integer is an ErrorCode value assigned when an integer argument is absent from the command line.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Invalid Integer">
  <data key="d0">Invalid Integer</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Invalid Integer is an ErrorCode value assigned when an integer argument cannot be parsed as an integer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marshalling Behavior">
  <data key="d0">Marshalling Behavior</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Marshalling Behavior is the process of converting stored command-line argument values into typed values such as boolean, string, and integer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Set Method">
  <data key="d0">Set Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Set Method is a method deployed into marshalers, declared abstract in ArgumentMarshaler, and updates marshaler state from a String parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;Set Method is the abstract method added to ArgumentMarshaler so that concrete marshalers can accept a String parameter and update their stored value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Get Method">
  <data key="d0">Get Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Get Method is a method deployed into marshalers, declared abstract in ArgumentMarshaler, and returns an Object value that callers cast to Boolean, String, or Integer.&lt;SEP&gt;Get Method is the method deployed into concrete ArgumentMarshaler derivatives so that values can be returned as Object and then cast by Args.&lt;SEP&gt;The get operation of Java.util.Map that retrieves an Object associated with a key.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-207d517b4dd92803d5557692307191fb-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-08.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604868</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="setInteger">
  <data key="d0">setInteger</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">setInteger is a method in ArgumentMarshaler that assigns an integer value to the integerValue field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="getInteger">
  <data key="d0">getInteger</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">getInteger is a method in ArgumentMarshaler that returns the stored integerValue.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598418</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="booleanArgs">
  <data key="d0">booleanArgs</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">booleanArgs is a field in the Args class that represents a map-like collection keyed by argument characters, identified by Character keys. Its described implementation and stored values vary across references, indicating either a historical change or distinct usages within Args. In one formulation, booleanArgs is a Map from Character to Boolean that stores declared and parsed Boolean argument values; it maps each argument character to its parsed boolean value and is initialized to false for boolean schema elements.

In another formulation, booleanArgs is a private Map or HashMap field in Args that stores ArgumentMarshaler instances for Boolean arguments, keyed by Character. In this role, it functions as a data collection of boolean argument marshalers rather than parsed boolean values, and one description notes that it previously held these Character-to-ArgumentMarshaler mappings before removal. Together, the descriptions identify booleanArgs as an internal Args structure associated with boolean arguments, either retaining parsed Boolean values or the marshalers used to process them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integer.parseInt">
  <data key="d0">Integer.parseInt</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Integer.parseInt is a Java standard method used by IntegerArgumentMarshaler to convert a String argument into an integer value.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer.parseInt is the standard Java static method invoked by setIntArg to convert a command-line parameter string to an integer.&lt;SEP&gt;Java method called by IntegerArgumentMarshaler to parse a string into an integer value.&lt;SEP&gt;Integer.parseInt is a Java method that converts a string into an integer value; Month.parse calls Integer.parseInt to interpret numeric month input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GetBoolean">
  <data key="d0">GetBoolean</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">GetBoolean is a public method in Args that retrieves a boolean argument by obtaining an ArgumentMarshaler and casting the Get Method result to Boolean.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BooleanValue">
  <data key="d0">BooleanValue</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">BooleanValue is a private boolean field in BooleanArgumentMarshaler that holds the boolean argument state after the variable is moved from ArgumentMarshaler.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
