<node id="Type-Case">
  <data key="d0">Type-Case</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anti-pattern criticized in setArgument, where control flow switches on argument type rather than calling a single marshaler operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Type-Case is the instanceof-based dispatch pattern in setArgument that selects helper methods by marshaler type and is removed during refactoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790598420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dirt">
  <data key="d0">Dirt</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design smell described when moving setIntArg would require passing two function arguments, args and currentArgument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-14.txt</data>
