  <data key="d0">testSimpleDoublePresent</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">testSimpleDoublePresent is a test method that creates an Args instance with schema x## and arguments -x 42.3, then asserts validity, cardinality, presence, and double value.&lt;SEP&gt;testSimpleDoublePresent is a Java test method that constructs an Args instance with the specification x## and the arguments -x 42.3, then asserts that the argument cardinality is 1, that the argument x is present, and that the double value for x is 42.3 within 0.001.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019</data>
