  <data key="d2">testInvalidDouble is a test method that creates an Args instance with schema x## and argument -x Forty two, then asserts invalid state and the expected double error message.&lt;SEP&gt;testInvalidDouble is a Java test method that constructs an Args instance with the specification x## and the invalid double argument Forty two, expects an ArgsException, and verifies that the exception reports INVALID_DOUBLE for argument x with parameter Forty two.</data>
