<node id="SerialDate Constructor">
  <data key="d0">SerialDate Constructor</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">SerialDate Constructor is the protected no-argument constructor for SerialDate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IsValid Weekday Code">
  <data key="d0">IsValid Weekday Code</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">IsValid Weekday Code is a static method in SerialDate that checks whether an integer code represents a valid day of the week by switching over weekday constants and returning true or false.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="String To Weekday Code">
  <data key="d0">String To Weekday Code</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">String To Weekday Code is a static method in SerialDate that converts a trimmed weekday string to an integer weekday code by comparing the string against short and full weekday names from Date Format Symbols, returning -1 when the string is not convertible.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weekday Code To String">
  <data key="d0">Weekday Code To String</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Weekday Code To String is a static method in SerialDate that converts an integer weekday code to a string weekday name using the weekday array supplied by Date Format Symbols.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Get Months">
  <data key="d0">Get Months</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Get Months is a static method in SerialDate that returns an array of month names, with an overloaded form that accepts a shortened flag and selects shortened or full month names from Date Format Symbols.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IsValid Month Code">
  <data key="d0">IsValid Month Code</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">IsValid Month Code is a static method in SerialDate that checks whether an integer code represents a valid month by switching over month constants and returning true or false.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Month Code To Quarter">
  <data key="d0">Month Code To Quarter</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Month Code To Quarter is a static method in SerialDate that maps a month code to a quarter of the year using month constants, with documentation indicating an IllegalArgumentException may be thrown for invalid input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Date Format Symbols">
  <data key="d0">Date Format Symbols</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Date Format Symbols is a referenced object that supplies arrays of short weekday names, full weekday names, short month names, and full month names used by SerialDate methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599006</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weekday Constants">
  <data key="d0">Weekday Constants</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Weekday Constants are symbolic integer constants such as SUNDAY, MONDAY, TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY, THURSDAY, FRIDAY, and SATURDAY used to validate weekday codes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Month Constants">
  <data key="d0">Month Constants</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Month Constants are symbolic integer constants such as JANUARY, FEBRUARY, MARCH, APRIL, MAY, JUNE, JULY, AUGUST, SEPTEMBER, OCTOBER, NOVEMBER, and DECEMBER used to validate and map month codes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weekday">
  <data key="d0">Weekday</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weekday is the abstract day-of-week value represented in SerialDate by integer codes, string names, and constant identifiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599009</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weekday Code">
  <data key="d0">Weekday Code</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Weekday Code is an integer value used by SerialDate to identify a weekday, and it is validated, converted from a string, or converted to a string.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Month Code">
  <data key="d0">Month Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Month Code is an integer code representing a month of the year, used by SerialDate.Java methods to convert to quarters, strings, and parsed from strings.&lt;SEP&gt;Month Code is an integer value used by SerialDate to identify a month, and the input specifies the month code range as 1 to 12.&lt;SEP&gt;Month Code is a numeric representation of a calendar month used by the tested conversion methods, with valid values implied by the tests to be 1 through 12.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Short Weekday Names">
  <data key="d0">Short Weekday Names</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Short Weekday Names are abbreviated weekday name values obtained from Date Format Symbols and used by String To Weekday Code for conversion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weekday Names">
  <data key="d0">Weekday Names</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Weekday Names are full weekday name values obtained from Date Format Symbols and used by String To Weekday Code and Weekday Code To String.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Month Names">
  <data key="d0">Month Names</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Month Names are full month name arrays returned by Get Months and obtained from Date Format Symbols.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shortened Month Names">
  <data key="d0">Shortened Month Names</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Shortened Month Names are abbreviated month name arrays returned by Get Months when the shortened flag is true and obtained from Date Format Symbols.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isValidWeekInMonthCode">
  <data key="d0">isValidWeekInMonthCode</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">isValidWeekInMonthCode is a static method in SerialDate.Java that checks whether an integer code represents a valid week-in-month value.&lt;SEP&gt;isValidWeekInMonthCode is a static method in SerialDate that returns true when an integer code matches a valid week-in-month constant and false otherwise.&lt;SEP&gt;isValidWeekInMonthCode is a function called in testIsValidWeekInMonthCode that validates week-in-month codes, with the visible tests expecting true for 0 through 4 and false for 5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DATE_FORMAT_SYMBOLS">
  <data key="d0">DATE_FORMAT_SYMBOLS</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">DATE_FORMAT_SYMBOLS is a date format symbols object referenced in SerialDate.Java to obtain arrays of long and short month names for month conversion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599013</data>
