</node>
<node id="Day-Of-The-Week">
  <data key="d0">Day-Of-The-Week</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Day-Of-The-Week is the calendar weekday concept encoded by target weekday codes and used to compare, select, and adjust dates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Years">
  <data key="d0">Years</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Years is the numeric count of years to add to a base date in the addYears method, with negative values permitted.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Day-Of-Month">
  <data key="d0">Day-Of-Month</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Day-Of-Month is the calendar date component represented by day values such as dd, baseD, and targetD, and clamped against the last valid day of a month.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Year">
  <data key="d0">Year</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Year is the calendar year component retrieved from a base date or calculated as targetY and used in last-day-of-month and date construction calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Math.abs">
  <data key="d0">Math.abs</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Math.abs is a static Java utility method invoked to compute an absolute numeric difference in weekday calculations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
