<node id="Create Instance">
  <data key="d0">Create Instance</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Create Instance is a static factory method in SerialDate with overloads that returns a SpreadsheetDate instance created from day, month, and year values, a serial number, or a Java Date.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Get End Of Current Month">
  <data key="d0">Get End Of Current Month</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Get End Of Current Month is a SerialDate method that rolls a base date forward to the last day of that month and returns a new SerialDate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Week In Month To String">
  <data key="d0">Week In Month To String</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Week In Month To String is a static SerialDate method that converts a week-in-month integer code into a descriptive string such as First, Second, Third, Fourth, or Last.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599048</data>
