<node id="Microsoft Support Article Q181370">
  <data key="d0">Microsoft Support Article Q181370</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft support article Q181370, referenced by a Microsoft website URL, that provides information about Microsoft Excel's deliberate 1900 leap-year bug.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="29 February 1900">
  <data key="d0">29 February 1900</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A nonexistent calendar date that Excel treats as an extra day due to the deliberate 1900 leap-year bug.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="calcOrdinal">
  <data key="d0">calcOrdinal</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">calcOrdinal is a private SpreadsheetDate method that computes an ordinal day from day, month, and year using leap-year information and aggregate month-day values.&lt;SEP&gt;A SpreadsheetDate method invoked with day, month, and year to compute the ordinal day value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="huntForMonthContaining">
  <data key="d0">huntForMonthContaining</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">huntForMonthContaining is a private SpreadsheetDate method that identifies the month containing an ordinal day within a year.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="daysBeforeThisMonth">
  <data key="d0">daysBeforeThisMonth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">daysBeforeThisMonth is a private SpreadsheetDate method that returns the aggregate days before a month, adjusted for leap-year status.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="huntForYearContaining">
  <data key="d0">huntForYearContaining</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">huntForYearContaining is a private SpreadsheetDate method that identifies the year containing an ordinal day.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="firstOrdinalOfYear">
  <data key="d0">firstOrdinalOfYear</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">firstOrdinalOfYear is a private SpreadsheetDate method that returns the ordinal day of January 1 for a given year by calling calcOrdinal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b96a37e68a1f0fd9f9aae3b5629b124f-chunk-044</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-18.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790599080</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
