<node id="Add">
  <data key="d0">Add</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Add is a method name that may be consistent for math addition but can become a pun when used for a different semantic operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Insert">
  <data key="d0">Insert</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Insert is a method name proposed as a clearer alternative to Add when the operation inserts a parameter into a collection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Append">
  <data key="d0">Append</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Append is a method name proposed as a clearer alternative to Add when the operation appends a value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Don't Pun">
  <data key="d0">Don't Pun</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Don't Pun is a naming principle advising against using the same word for two different purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solution Domain Names">
  <data key="d0">Solution Domain Names</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solution Domain Names is a naming approach that uses computer science, algorithm, pattern, and math terms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Problem Domain Names">
  <data key="d0">Problem Domain Names</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problem Domain Names is a naming approach that uses problem-domain terms when no standard programmer term exists.&lt;SEP&gt;Names drawn from the problem domain and used in code when no programmer-eese exists for the activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
