<node id="Don't Be Cute">
  <data key="d0">Don't Be Cute</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Don't Be Cute is a naming guideline section that advises against clever, slang, or culture-dependent names.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clarity Over Cleverness">
  <data key="d0">Clarity Over Cleverness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clarity Over Cleverness is the principle stated in Don't Be Cute that clear names are preferable to clever names.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Colloquialisms Or Slang">
  <data key="d0">Colloquialisms Or Slang</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Colloquialisms Or Slang are forms of cuteness in code, such as Whack and EatMyShorts, that the naming guidance discourages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistent Lexicon">
  <data key="d0">Consistent Lexicon</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consistent Lexicon is a consistent set of naming words that helps programmers understand code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collection">
  <data key="d0">Collection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Collection is a data-structure context for the naming example where Insert or Append is clearer than Add.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solution Domain">
  <data key="d0">Solution Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solution Domain is the technical programming domain whose terms are recommended for names when programmers already know the concepts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Problem Domain">
  <data key="d0">Problem Domain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The source of names for code elements when no programmer-eese exists for the task.&lt;SEP&gt;Problem Domain is the specific business or problem context whose names are recommended when no programmer term exists.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f209a7a16ee116e66dcaca0799c06baa-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-02.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603332</data>
