<node id="Routine">
  <data key="d0">Routine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A programming construct mentioned in the early days of programming, alongside subroutines, as used to compose systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Routine is a unit of code that is read to judge whether code is clean because the routine behaves as expected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d58f62a4832abf3c8bbf730215895c6d-chunk-004</data>
