  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Stepdown Rule is the principle that code should read as a top-down narrative with each function followed by functions at the next lower level of abstraction.&lt;SEP&gt;A readability principle that helps the program read like a newspaper article.</data>
