<node id="Point">
  <data key="d0">Point</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Point is a class instantiated with new Point(0,0) and described as naturally taking two ordered components of a single value.&lt;SEP&gt;A class used to group coordinate values such as x and y into a single conceptual argument in makeCircle.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java class or interface representing a point on the Cartesian plane, appearing in concrete and abstract forms.&lt;SEP&gt;Point is a coordinate data type used as a top-left position for Square and Rectangle and as a center position for Circle.&lt;SEP&gt;A class in a code example representing a point with coordinates used by MetricsCalculator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf9b0cb392cf6be9fae672222887f4bd-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cf9b0cb392cf6be9fae672222887f4bd-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-06.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-07.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604703</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pageData">
  <data key="d0">pageData</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">pageData is the argument passed to SetupTeardownIncluder.render(pageData) to represent data to be rendered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="outputStream">
  <data key="d0">outputStream</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">outputStream is an argument used in the dyadic writeField(outputStream, name) call.&lt;SEP&gt;An output stream object that can receive writeField as a member method or be held as a member variable to reduce function arguments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="name">
  <data key="d0">name</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">name is an argument variable used in the writeField example and is discussed as lacking natural cohesion and ordering with output stream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="isSuite">
  <data key="d0">isSuite</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">isSuite is the boolean parameter in the render method example, shown as render(boolean isSuite), and illustrates a flag argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="boolean">
  <data key="d0">boolean</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">boolean is the data type used for flag arguments, such as the boolean value passed to render in the render(boolean isSuite) example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MyFile">
  <data key="d0">MyFile</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">MyFile is the file-name string literal used in the fileExists and fileOpen examples as a single argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cartesian Point">
  <data key="d0">Cartesian Point</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cartesian Point is a mathematical point that naturally takes two arguments representing ordered coordinate components of a single value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dyad">
  <data key="d0">Dyad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A function that takes two arguments, discussed as requiring attention to argument ordering and possible refactoring into monadic form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monad">
  <data key="d0">Monad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A function that takes one argument, presented as a target form for reducing dyadic functions and for monadic variable-argument functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triad">
  <data key="d0">Triad</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A function that takes three arguments, described as significantly harder to understand than dyads because of ordering, pausing, and ignoring issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FieldWriter">
  <data key="d0">FieldWriter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A proposed extracted class that accepts outputStream in its constructor and provides a write method to reduce argument passing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="write">
  <data key="d0">write</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of FieldWriter used to perform writing through the encapsulated outputStream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expected">
  <data key="d0">Expected</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An argument convention representing the value against which actual results are compared in assertion functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actual">
  <data key="d0">Actual</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An argument convention representing the value produced by code under test in assertion functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Floating Point Equality">
  <data key="d0">Floating Point Equality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The relative comparison of floating-point values, illustrated by an assertEquals overload with a tolerance argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="makeCircle">
  <data key="d0">makeCircle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A function used to contrast argument-object wrapping, shown with individual coordinate arguments and with a Point center argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Argument Objects">
  <data key="d0">Argument Objects</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A refactoring idea in which groups of related function arguments are wrapped into a class of their own to reduce argument count.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Argument Lists">
  <data key="d0">Argument Lists</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The use of a variable number of arguments passed to a function, exemplified by String.format and equivalent to a single list argument when treated identically.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Keyword Form">
  <data key="d0">Keyword Form</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A function naming form that encodes argument names into the function name to clarify argument order and intent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="assertExpectedEqualsActual">
  <data key="d0">assertExpectedEqualsActual</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A proposed better-named assertion function that makes the expected and actual argument order explicit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Side Effects">
  <data key="d0">Side Effects</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hidden changes made by a function beyond its promised behavior, described as deceptive and capable of causing temporal coupling and order dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UserValidator">
  <data key="d0">UserValidator</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A class containing checkPassword and a Cryptographer member, used to illustrate a function with a side effect.&lt;SEP&gt;UserValidator is a Java class shown in the code listing that validates a user password using a UserGateway and Cryptographer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="checkPassword">
  <data key="d0">checkPassword</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of UserValidator that matches a userName to a password, returns a Boolean result, and is stated to have a side effect.&lt;SEP&gt;checkPassword is a function in UserValidator that receives a user name and password, returns a Boolean result, and calls Session.initialize when validation succeeds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UserGateway">
  <data key="d0">UserGateway</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A gateway class used in checkPassword to find a User by name.&lt;SEP&gt;UserGateway is a collaborator used by checkPassword to find a User by name.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="findByName">
  <data key="d0">findByName</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A method of UserGateway that locates a User using a userName.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cryptographer">
  <data key="d0">Cryptographer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A private member of UserValidator that is presumably used for password-related cryptographic operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Cryptographer is a collaborator in UserValidator used to decrypt a coded phrase with a password.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Argument Ordering">
  <data key="d0">Argument Ordering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The sequence in which function arguments are passed or remembered, emphasized for dyads, triads, and assertion methods where expected, actual, and message order can be confusing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Verb-Noun Pair">
  <data key="d0">Verb-Noun Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A function naming pattern in which a function name and the corresponding argument form a verb and noun pair, exemplified by write(name).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field">
  <data key="d0">Field</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A named attribute or conceptual attribute, exemplified by the field written by writeField and by a class field that can hold outputStream.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parameter">
  <data key="d0">Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A value passed into a function that may be changed by side effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Globals">
  <data key="d0">System Globals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Global variables or state that a function may inadvertently change, contributing to side effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Class Variables">
  <data key="d0">Class Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Variables belonging to the class that owns a function and may be changed unexpectedly by side effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Order Dependency">
  <data key="d0">Order Dependency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A dependency on execution order that can result from side effects in functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Password Matching Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Password Matching Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard algorithm used to match a userName to a password in the UserValidator example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UserValidator.java">
  <data key="d0">UserValidator.java</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A code listing that contains the UserValidator class and the checkPassword method.&lt;SEP&gt;UserValidator.java is the code listing that contains the UserValidator class.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Class">
  <data key="d0">Current Class</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The class in which outputStream can be held as a member variable or field to reduce argument passing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
