<node id="Object Oriented Programming">
  <data key="d0">Object Oriented Programming</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Object Oriented Programming is a programming paradigm in which a function can change the state of its owning object, reducing the need for output arguments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Owning Object">
  <data key="d0">Owning Object</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Owning Object is the object whose state should be changed when a function must modify something, instead of using an output argument.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
