<node id="Error Handling">
  <data key="d0">Error Handling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Error Handling is the activity of processing failures, exceptions, or error conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Error handling is the programming practice of detecting and responding to abnormal inputs, device failures, and other unexpected conditions while preserving intended behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Error handling is a separate concern from main logic that supports reasoning about code and maintainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Error Handling is a complete strategy for managing errors in clean code.&lt;SEP&gt;Error Handling is a discipline of paying attention to details; complete error handling is required for clean code, while abbreviated error handling glosses over details.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d58f62a4832abf3c8bbf730215895c6d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d58f62a4832abf3c8bbf730215895c6d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-07.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-01.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606209</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dependency Magnet">
  <data key="d0">Dependency Magnet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dependency Magnet is a design problem in which many classes depend on one class, increasing recompilation and redeployment pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
