<node id="Redeployment">
  <data key="d0">Redeployment</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Redeployment is the deployment activity that is forced on dependent classes when the Error enum changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Catch/Finally Block">
  <data key="d0">Catch/Finally Block</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Catch/Finally Block is the error or final handling block after which no code should appear if a function contains a try keyword.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Try Keyword">
  <data key="d0">Try Keyword</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Try Keyword is the keyword for a try block; if present in a Function, the keyword should be the very first word.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Processing">
  <data key="d0">Normal Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal Processing is the happy-path behavior mixed with error processing by Try/Catch Blocks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790603783</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Happy Path Code">
  <data key="d0">Happy Path Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Happy Path Code is the successful-processing code from which error processing can be separated when exceptions are used.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-03.txt</data>
