</node>
<node id="Domain-specific Language">
  <data key="d0">Domain-specific Language</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Language designed by programmers to describe a system, built from functions and classes, and used to tell the story of the system.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain-specific language is a higher-level or specialized language used to express specifications, and the Clean Code chapter treats such specifications as code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-70106d3c6c60a2a04b530f45336de970-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d58f62a4832abf3c8bbf730215895c6d-chunk-000</data>
