<node id="Javadocs">
  <data key="d0">Javadocs</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Javadocs are documentation entries for Java public APIs, including those for the standard Java library, and can be helpful but also misleading.&lt;SEP&gt;A documentation comment style referenced in the input, described as potentially noisy and redundant, with examples that serve no purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;Javadocs are Java documentation comments or generated documentation pages, described as useful for public APIs and anathema to nonpublic code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-04.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public API">
  <data key="d0">Public API</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Public API is a publicly exposed software interface for which good Javadocs should be written.&lt;SEP&gt;Application programming interface exposed to callers; the input also advises against returning or accepting certain class families as arguments to public APIs.&lt;SEP&gt;A publicly exposed application interface that should avoid returning or accepting boundary interfaces directly.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-207d517b4dd92803d5557692307191fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-207d517b4dd92803d5557692307191fb-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-04.txt&lt;SEP&gt;chapter-08.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604868</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Java Library">
  <data key="d0">Standard Java Library</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard Java Library is the standard Java library whose Javadocs are described as helpful and satisfying for writing Java programs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-04.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bad Comments">
  <data key="d0">Bad Comments</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bad Comments are comments that usually serve as crutches or excuses for poor code or insufficient decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ecee1e439eb5fb52d346911e1683e490-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-04.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604159</data>
