  <data key="d2">Horizontal Openness and Density is a code-formatting principle that uses horizontal white space to associate strongly related elements and disassociate weakly related elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ae06dfc90c814559f684ae92cc598260-chunk-003</data>
