<node id="Null Check">
  <data key="d0">Null Check</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A code technique that tests whether a value or object reference is null before using that value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-07.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604703</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Returning Null">
  <data key="d0">Returning Null</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A method design practice in which a method returns null, which the text describes as creating work and problems for callers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-07.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604703</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Passing Null">
  <data key="d0">Passing Null</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A caller practice in which null is supplied as an argument to a method, which the text describes as worse than returning null.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-07.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604703</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Special Case Object">
  <data key="d0">Special Case Object</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A non-null object representing a special condition, suggested as an alternative to returning null.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-07.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604703</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Empty List">
  <data key="d0">Empty List</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A predefined immutable list with no elements, returned by Java's Collections.emptyList() and used to avoid returning null.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-98268aa1e2e5692cb0faaf2b6fae4a09-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-07.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790604703</data>
