<node id="Java 5 Annotations">
  <data key="d0">Java 5 Annotations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Java language mechanism used to simplify configuration, annotate entity details, and reduce explicit wiring logic.&lt;SEP&gt;Java 5 Annotations are annotation constructs used to define aspects in pure Java code within the AspectJ Annotation Form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f8b0f36a5c42d0808fec00a058082be8-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f8b0f36a5c42d0808fec00a058082be8-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-11.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790605586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AOP">
  <data key="d0">AOP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspect-oriented programming approach whose real value is specifying systemic behaviors concisely and modularly; sometimes confused with implementation techniques such as method interception and proxies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f8b0f36a5c42d0808fec00a058082be8-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-11.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790605586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
