  <data key="d2">Test Get Page Hierarchy As Xml is a test method in SerializedPageResponderTest that issues a request for a page hierarchy and asserts that the response should be XML.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Test Get Page Hierarchy Has Right Tags">
  <data key="d0">Test Get Page Hierarchy Has Right Tags</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Test Get Page Hierarchy Has Right Tags is a test method in SerializedPageResponderTest that issues a request for a page hierarchy and asserts that the response contains specific name tags.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RSpec">
  <data key="d0">RSpec</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">RSpec is a reference cited in a footnote next to the mention of the given-when-then convention.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Last Day Of Month Rule">
  <data key="d0">Last Day Of Month Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Last Day Of Month Rule is a general rule derived from the Add Months tests: incrementing the month must not produce a date beyond the last day of that month.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F.I.R.S.T.">
  <data key="d0">F.I.R.S.T.</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">F.I.R.S.T. is an acronym representing five clean test rules: Fast, Independent, Repeatable, Self-Validating, and Timely.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fast Test Rule">
  <data key="d0">Fast Test Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast Test Rule states that tests should run quickly so that tests are executed frequently and problems are found early.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Independent Test Rule">
  <data key="d0">Independent Test Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Independent Test Rule states that tests should not depend on each other and can be run in any order without cascading failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Repeatable Test Rule">
  <data key="d0">Repeatable Test Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Repeatable Test Rule states that tests should be repeatable in any environment, including production, QA, and offline laptop environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Validating Test Rule">
  <data key="d0">Self-Validating Test Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Self-Validating Test Rule states that tests should produce a boolean output indicating whether they pass or fail without manual inspection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Timely Test Rule">
  <data key="d0">Timely Test Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Timely Test Rule states that unit tests should be written just before the production code that makes them pass.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Project Health">
  <data key="d0">Project Health</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Project Health is the overall condition of a project that is influenced by both tests and production code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domain-Specific Language">
  <data key="d0">Domain-Specific Language</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Domain-Specific Language is a language-like representation used by testing APIs to support test writing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boolean Output">
  <data key="d0">Boolean Output</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Boolean Output is a pass/fail result that self-validating tests should produce.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Month Increment">
  <data key="d0">Month Increment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Month Increment is the operation of increasing the month in a date while respecting the last day of the month.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="February 28th">
  <data key="d0">February 28th</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">February 28th is a date used as an example input for a month increment operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="March 28th">
  <data key="d0">March 28th</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">March 28th is the expected date produced by incrementing the month from February 28th.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tested Concept">
  <data key="d0">Tested Concept</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tested Concept is a concept or behavior that a test function tests individually.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Object Mentor Training Materials">
  <data key="d0">Object Mentor Training Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Object Mentor Training Materials is the source cited for the F.I.R.S.T. acronym.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
