<node id="Missing Month Increment Test">
  <data key="d0">Missing Month Increment Test</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Missing Month Increment Test is a useful test that is not present and would test incrementing the month from February 28th to March 28th.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Rule">
  <data key="d0">General Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">General Rule is a general rule hidden amidst miscellaneous tests that describes how month increments constrain dates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Miscellaneous Tests">
  <data key="d0">Miscellaneous Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Miscellaneous Tests are assorted tests in which a general rule about month increments is hidden.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One Concept Per Test Rule">
  <data key="d0">One Concept Per Test Rule</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One Concept Per Test Rule is the rule to test just one concept per test function and minimize the number of asserts per concept.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Downstream Failures">
  <data key="d0">Downstream Failures</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Downstream Failures are cascading test failures that occur when tests depend on one another and an earlier test fails.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">Diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnosis is the process of identifying the cause of test failures, which is made difficult by dependent tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Downstream Defects">
  <data key="d0">Downstream Defects</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Downstream Defects are defects that can be hidden when dependent tests cause cascading failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="QA Environment">
  <data key="d0">QA Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">QA Environment is an environment in which repeatable tests should be able to run.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Log File">
  <data key="d0">Log File</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Log File is a file that self-validating tests should not require a person to read in order to determine whether tests pass.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text Files">
  <data key="d0">Text Files</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Text Files are different files that self-validating tests should not require a person to manually compare in order to determine whether tests pass.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Manual Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual Evaluation is a long manual assessment that self-validating tests should avoid requiring when determining test results.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Behavior Driven Development">
  <data key="d0">Behavior Driven Development</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Behavior Driven Development is a software development approach indicated by the title of the RSpec book.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gamma et al.">
  <data key="d0">Gamma et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma et al. is the author group listed for the Design Patterns book.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e6b59836a05af0c112c0d24b77e2c123-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-09.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606383</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chapter 10: Classes">
  <data key="d0">Chapter 10: Classes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A chapter that discusses clean classes, class organization, encapsulation, and the rule that classes should be small.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clean Classes">
  <data key="d0">Clean Classes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A quality goal for class design that requires attention to higher levels of code organization beyond statements and functions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Class Organization">
  <data key="d0">Class Organization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The arrangement of class variables and functions that follows Java conventions, placing variables before functions and public functions before private utilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public Static Constants">
  <data key="d0">Public Static Constants</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of class variables that should appear first in a class according to class organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Private Static Variables">
  <data key="d0">Private Static Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of class variables that should appear after public static constants in class organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Private Instance Variables">
  <data key="d0">Private Instance Variables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of class variables that should appear after private static variables in class organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Private Utilities">
  <data key="d0">Private Utilities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Private helper functions that are placed immediately after the public function that calls them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classes Should Be Small">
  <data key="d0">Classes Should Be Small</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A rule that classes should be small, with smaller being better than small, and class size measured by responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SuperDashboard">
  <data key="d0">SuperDashboard</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Java class extending JFrame and implementing MetaDataUser. SuperDashboard exposes methods for dragging, title, IdeMenuBar, MetaObject helper display, Component focus, and version/build numbers. The class is described as having too many responsibilities despite a small method count.&lt;SEP&gt;A Java class in Listing 10-1 that extends JFrame, implements MetaDataUser, and exposes about 70 public methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="God Class">
  <data key="d0">God Class</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A term for an excessively large or over-responsible class, as some developers might call SuperDashboard.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
