<node id="Cohesion">
  <data key="d0">Cohesion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A software design concept describing classes with a small number of instance variables. Methods of a class should manipulate one or more of those variables, and manipulating more variables indicates more cohesion to the class.&lt;SEP&gt;A property of a class in which its methods and variables are co-dependent and function as a logical whole, with high cohesion indicating strong internal consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Version Information">
  <data key="d0">Version Information</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured data consisting of major version number, minor version number, and build number. Version Information is tracked by SuperDashboard and encapsulated by Version.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
