  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reason To Change">
  <data key="d0">Reason To Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Reason To Change is a rationale for modifying a class or module. The Single Responsibility Principle equates a single responsibility with one and only one reason to change.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abstractions">
  <data key="d0">Abstractions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Abstractions are code structures or concepts that can be recognized and created by identifying responsibilities or reasons to change in code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Class Name">
  <data key="d0">Class Name</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Class Name is the name of a class. A concise class name should describe the responsibilities fulfilled by the class and helps determine class size, while ambiguity hints at too many responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weasel Words">
  <data key="d0">Weasel Words</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weasel Words are ambiguous class-name terms such as Processor, Manager, or Super. They often hint at unfortunate aggregation of responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Programming Activities">
  <data key="d0">Programming Activities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Programming Activities are activities of programming, including getting software to work and making software clean. Developers may focus on getting code to work rather than organization and cleanliness.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Class">
  <data key="d0">Small Class</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A class with a single responsibility, a single reason to change, and collaboration with a few other classes to achieve system behaviors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
