<node id="Single Reason To Change">
  <data key="d0">Single Reason To Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Single Reason To Change is a design principle in which a class has one reason to change, as attributed to each small class in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large Class">
  <data key="d0">Large Class</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large Class is a class composition alternative contrasted with many small classes, described as undesirable in the opening design point.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prime Number">
  <data key="d0">Prime Number</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prime Number is a mathematical number that the PrintPrimes program computes and lists in the example.&lt;SEP&gt;Prime Number is a mathematical number that the PrimeGenerator class generates as part of prime number generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="First M Prime Numbers">
  <data key="d0">First M Prime Numbers</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">First M Prime Numbers is the output data set produced by PrintPrimes, consisting of the first M prime numbers printed page by page.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PrimePrinter">
  <data key="d0">PrimePrinter</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">PrimePrinter is a Java class in the literatePrimes package. The PrimePrinter main method configures the number of primes and row/column page layout, then uses PrimeGenerator and RowColumnPagePrinter to print the first prime numbers.&lt;SEP&gt;PrimePrinter is a main program class that handles the execution environment for the prime number printing program and would change if the method of invocation changed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
  <data key="d5">1790606393</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
