  <data key="d0">Open-Closed Principle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Open-Closed Principle is an object-oriented design principle stating that classes should be open for extension but closed for modification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4482a25ecfcd0fad59918839a6f47f2a-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">chapter-10.txt</data>
