  <data key="d8">SerialDate defines the isInRange method.&lt;SEP&gt;SerialDate declares the abstract method isInRange, available in two-argument and three-argument forms, for testing whether a SerialDate value falls within a date range.&lt;SEP&gt;isInRange accepts two SerialDate boundary arguments that define a date range, with an optional integer inclusion flag controlling endpoint inclusion.&lt;SEP&gt;isInRange is a method declared within the SerialDate class.</data>
