<edge source="Args" target="ArgsException">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Args, ArgsException) describes a close exception-handling relationship in which Args uses ArgsException to signal failures in argument parsing or construction. Args methods declare that they throw ArgsException, and the class throws it when parsing a format string or command-line arguments fails, when required argument values are missing or invalid, and specifically when integer parameters or required double arguments are missing or invalid during parsing or construction.

Originally, Args contained a nested, private ArgsException class as part of its internal error-reporting structure. In that design, ArgsException represented argument-processing failures and was embedded within Args rather than being a standalone top-level class.

Subsequent refactoring separated this responsibility: code associated with ArgsException was moved out of Args and placed into a separate ArgsException module or class, allowing error support to be isolated from argument parsing. This reconciles descriptions of containment with descriptions of separation by reflecting an earlier nested implementation and a later modularized implementation.</data>
  <data key="d9">code moved,code movement,contains,declares,depends on,error,error handling,exception,exception handling,module separation,nested exception,refactoring,throws,uses</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d11">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d12">1790598607</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Args" target="ArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Args uses ArgumentMarshaler instances to handle argument values.&lt;SEP&gt;ArgumentMarshaler is added to Args as a private class and design concept.&lt;SEP&gt;ArgumentMarshaler is defined as a private class inside Args.&lt;SEP&gt;Args maintains a marshalers map whose values are ArgumentMarshaler instances for parsed schema elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Args declares the ArgumentMarshaler abstract class.&lt;SEP&gt;Args stores ArgumentMarshaler instances in the marshalers map.&lt;SEP&gt;Args maintains a map of ArgumentMarshaler instances and uses them to marshal parsed argument values.</data>
