<edge source="Args" target="ErrorCode">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Args, ErrorCode) connects Args to an ErrorCode enumeration used for representing error states in argument parsing. The descriptions consistently characterize ErrorCode as an error-state enum associated with Args, and they indicate that Args uses its values to represent, record, and track parsing failures.

Specifically, Args is described as defining, declaring, or containing ErrorCode as a nested or inner enum, and as referencing ErrorCode values to record failure reasons and store the current parsing error state. In the same context, Args is said to store a value of ArgsException.ErrorCode in order to track the current error state and to reference ArgsException.ErrorCode values when constructing ArgsException instances during parsing.

The apparent discrepancy between ErrorCode being nested in Args and being identified as ArgsException.ErrorCode can be reconciled as a difference in naming or qualification: ErrorCode is the error enumeration used by Args, while ArgsException.ErrorCode is the more specific fully qualified reference to that enum when Args interacts with ArgsException. Under this reading, the relation captures Args' use of ErrorCode values for parsing-error bookkeeping and exception construction.</data>
  <data key="d9">contains,error model,error recording,error state,has_field,instance variable,references,uses</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
