  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">setIntArg throws ArgsException after recording an integer argument error.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg throws ArgsException after recording a missing or invalid integer argument.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg declares, catches, and rethrows ArgsException.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg throws ArgsException when an integer argument is missing or invalid.&lt;SEP&gt;setIntArg throws ArgsException when the next integer argument is missing or when conversion fails.</data>
