<edge source="ArgumentMarshaler" target="BooleanArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (ArgumentMarshaler, BooleanArgumentMarshaler) indicates that BooleanArgumentMarshaler is a concrete, specialized form of ArgumentMarshaler. It is described both as extending ArgumentMarshaler and as implementing the ArgumentMarshaler interface, which together show that it is a subtype conforming to the common argument-marshaling contract. Its primary responsibility is to provide the set and getValue behavior required for handling boolean argument values.

Within the Args class, BooleanArgumentMarshaler functions as a private class used specifically for boolean arguments. It is referenced in Args.setArgument as an instance of ArgumentMarshaler and can be identified through an instanceof check. It is also used as an ArgumentMarshaler entry in the marshalers map, where it supports the storage and retrieval of boolean argument values.</data>
  <data key="d9">class hierarchy,compatible type,extends,implements,inheritance,instanceof,interface implementation,is a,is a type of,is-a,specialization,subtype,type</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d12">1790598585</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="ArgumentMarshaler" target="StringArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">For the relation (ArgumentMarshaler, StringArgumentMarshaler), StringArgumentMarshaler is a specialized form of ArgumentMarshaler used in argument-handling contexts. It is described both as extending and implementing ArgumentMarshaler, and in either case it inherits or realizes the common marshaling interface associated with ArgumentMarshaler.

Within Args, StringArgumentMarshaler functions as an ArgumentMarshaler specifically for String arguments. It supplies the set and getValue behavior required for String values, is used in the marshalers map to handle string argument values, and is referenced as an ArgumentMarshaler instance in the Args.setArgument method. In that method, an instanceof check identifies StringArgumentMarshaler as a kind of ArgumentMarshaler, confirming its role as the String-specific marshaling component within the broader ArgumentMarshaler abstraction.</data>
  <data key="d9">class hierarchy,compatible type,extends,implements,inheritance,instanceof,interface implementation,is a,is a type of,is-a,specialization,subtype,type</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d12">1790598627</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="ArgumentMarshaler" target="IntegerArgumentMarshaler">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (ArgumentMarshaler, IntegerArgumentMarshaler) describes a subtype relationship in which IntegerArgumentMarshaler is a specialized form of ArgumentMarshaler. It is described both as implementing the ArgumentMarshaler interface and as extending ArgumentMarshaler to inherit the common marshaling interface, so the descriptions may reflect either an interface/implementation distinction or an abstract-parent class characterization. In either case, IntegerArgumentMarshaler is an ArgumentMarshaler derivative specifically intended for integer arguments.

Functionally, IntegerArgumentMarshaler provides the set and getValue behavior used to handle integer argument values. It is used by the Args class as an ArgumentMarshaler, including within a marshalers map that stores or retrieves marshalers for integer arguments. In Args.setArgument, IntegerArgumentMarshaler is referenced as an ArgumentMarshaler instance and is identified as that kind of marshaler through an instanceof check. It is also explicitly declared or characterized as a class extending ArgumentMarshaler, reinforcing its role as a concrete integer-specific implementation of the broader marshaling contract.</data>
  <data key="d9">class hierarchy,compatible type,derivative,extends,implements,inheritance,instanceof,interface implementation,is a,is a type of,is-a,specialization,subtype,type</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ff1f4d3804316cc277d01b65a1e72073-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">chapter-14.txt</data>
  <data key="d12">1790598672</data>
